<?xml version='1.0' standalone='yes'?>

<PLUGIN name="unraid-aicliagents" author="John White" version="2026.11.09.04" launch="Settings/AICliAgentsManager" pluginURL="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/johnpwhite/unraid-plg-aicliagents/main/unraid-aicliagents.plg" min="7.2.0" support="https://forums.unraid.net/topic/197460-plugin-support-unraid-tab-for-ai-cli-coding-agents-gemini-cli-claude-code-opencode-kilo-code-pi-coder-codex-cli-factory-droid-cli-copilot-nano-coder/" icon="assets/icons/google-gemini.png">

<CHANGES>
## 2026.11.09.04

**Agents and workspaces**

- **Feat: an agent can send a direct command to a helper it started, with your approval.** For example, it can open the helper's model menu. The Activity tray and an Unraid notification ask you: Allow once, Always allow for those two workspaces, or Block. You can see and remove the saved rules in the helper's menu.
- **Improve: text that another workspace types into a helper now shows who sent it.**
- **Feat: an OpenCode 2 helper can work without permission questions and gets its task when it starts.** This needs the setting "Let sub-agents run without asking".
- **Fix: running agents no longer look busy on newer Unraid kernels,** so dictated text, Relay messages, Continue and a helper's first task reach the agent again.

**Script runs**

- **Feat: scripts can start agents as a restricted user that sees only the folders you allow** (Settings, Script runs). A script that was approved before this update keeps running as root when it names no user.
- **Fix: the finish step of a script run reports errors correctly.**

**Storage**

- **Fix: a home backup that a plugin update or restart interrupts runs once more,** so the day's backup is not lost. A second interruption ends it and records the reason.

**Config Hub and Notebook**

- **Fix: the Config drift list keeps keyboard focus when it loads again.**
- **Fix: Notebook buttons, table filter chips and heading links are full size and easy to tap on a touch screen.**

## 2026.11.07.03

**Dictation**

- **Fix: "Send when I stop talking" works with live dictation, and when you tick it during a dictation.** Before, the option did nothing with live dictation, and a tick during a dictation took effect only at the next one. The terminal also keeps the keyboard focus while you dictate, so the text goes where you expect.

**Agents and workspaces**

- **Fix: an agent that keeps stopping with an error waits for you after three tries in a row,** instead of restarting every few seconds without end.
- **Feat: a closed helper workspace shows a Start button.** Selecting it starts nothing until you press Start, so looking at a helper no longer spends quota.
- **Improve: when the plugin refuses an agent action, it shows one plain sentence** with the workspace names and the real reason.
- **Fix: closing the last OpenCode 2 workspace stops its background service,** so no server process is left running.
- **Fix: a usage limit on one OpenCode provider no longer blocks a helper that uses another provider.**
- **Fix: the Beta version list no longer comes up empty** when a preview came out just before a stable release.
- **Fix: uninstalling an agent keeps a version that a process still uses,** and an agent cannot start while it is being uninstalled.

**Script runs**

- **Fix: the Notebook card of a finished script run is easy to find.** The tray has an Open note button, the card shows the run's title and the whole report, and a run in a project folder also gets a card in that project's Notebook.

**Storage, shutdown and Activity tray**

- **Fix: a home folder that you removed stays removed.** Before, it could come back on the boot disk when a workspace was still starting or a save was still running.
- **Fix: the plugin mounts and starts nothing while the server shuts down,** and an open page stops retrying.
- **Fix: a notice in the Activity tray stays until you close it,** instead of going away when the page refreshes.
- **Fix: buttons, menus and toggles on a phone are large enough to tap with a finger.**

**Scheduled jobs**

- **Feat: each scheduled job keeps a record of its last run,** and `jobs-status` lists every job as OK, warning, failed, skipped, late or missing. A monitoring tool can read it with no extra setup.

**Agent Store**

- **Fix: release notes load again for Codex** and other agents with large GitHub releases. When notes cannot be loaded, the window says so instead of saying there are none.
- **Fix: a first install of an agent says "Installing" in the Activity tray,** not "Upgrading".
- **Fix: in a diff note, the list of changed files is easy to tap on a phone.**

## 2026.11.04.02

**Agent Relay**

- **Fix: Relay notices stop repeating once you read the messages.** Before, a notice for a message that was already read came back every 30 seconds.
- **Feat: a Relay remote has a Copy setup prompt button.** Paste its one line into Claude Code or Codex on another computer, and that agent connects with no hand-copied keys.

**Helper workspaces**

- **Feat: helper workspaces follow one rule for every agent kind.** A helper's worktree is in a folder that git ignores, it can check out only the folders it needs, and its task file says how to use its branch. A merged and clean worktree is removed when the helper closes. A helper that fails to start leaves nothing behind.
- **Improve: OpenCode and Gemini CLI helpers can run without asking.** An agent may close a helper it created, and you get a notice instead of a question.
- **Fix: an agent can answer or reject the OpenCode permission box of its helper while a spinner moves above it.** To allow, the mark must be on Allow once.
- **Fix: a helper that was already stopped no longer gets a notice that it passed its time limit.** A helper that ended by itself is reported as no longer running.
- **Fix: a helper's task words are no longer replaced by piped input,** and a repository with no remote no longer tells the helper to push.

**Agents and secrets**

- **Fix: uninstalling an agent frees its disk space.**
- **Fix: two changes to agent keys at the same time no longer overwrite each other.** The vault shows a notice when it cannot save.
- **Fix: a damaged secrets or variables file no longer goes unnoticed.** The workspace editor shows a note, and every save sends one notification that names the kept copy.

**Scheduled jobs**

- **Fix: the scheduled home backup job waits for the backup to end and reports the real result.** Its output ends with one plain line, so a job report page or a phone push is readable. On a failure the line says what failed and what to do.

**Settings, Notebook and speed**

- **Fix: the Settings page no longer jumps to the top or loses keyboard focus while a storage warning shows.** A closed card stays closed, and the storage boxes keep showing the real state after a storage change.
- **Feat: when the Notebook is on, every agent is told to commit Notebook files with its other work in a git repo,** to check them for secrets first, and to ask before a push to a public remote.
- **Improve: every plugin request starts faster,** because it loads only the code it uses.

## 2026.11.02.02

**Scheduled jobs: please make a backup or check your schedule after this update**

- **Fix: scheduled jobs now really run.** The automatic home backup, the daily agent update check and the health check never fired on any server, because the schedule was written to a place the server does not read. Your backup schedule starts to work after this update with no change from you. Check the time of your last backup on the backup screen, and make one by hand if it is old.
- **Feat: each scheduled job can report its result** to a command you choose (setting `job_report_command`). With the setting empty, jobs run as normal. The backup job reports when the backup is queued, not when it ends, so check the backup screen for the result of the backup.

**Workspaces and agents**

- **Fix: saving workspaces from two places at once can no longer lose a change.** If a save cannot start within 10 seconds, it fails with a message.
- **Fix: the space check before an agent update counts real disk use.** On a compressed flash drive it no longer refuses an update that fits.
- **Fix: remounting an agent with no saved changes no longer writes a kernel warning** ("upperdir is in-use") to the system log.

## 2026.11.01.02

**Storage: please read if you change the storage engine**

- **Fix: changing a home from plain folders back to compressed layers keeps all your work.** Before, a change back within 14 days of the first change could delete the plain folder and still report success. If you changed a home to plain folders and back in that time, check its contents.
- **Fix: an interrupted storage change can always be continued or put back.** Before, a restart during a change could leave the page stuck, or **Put back** could make a half-copied home the live one.
- **Fix: Storage Apply does only what you asked.** A change that only saves the setting now only saves it, with no dialog. The work runs in the background, only the kind that changes is locked, and workspaces and storage actions wait during a move.
- **Improve: a stored home with no matching user on the server is reported** on the Storage card. It is not counted and it is not converted.

**Agents**

- **Improve: changing an agent's version takes a few minutes** instead of 16 to 21 on a busy server.
- **Fix: closing Factory saves its state.**
- **Fix: Config Hub never writes through a linked folder.**

**Terminal and Health**

- **Fix: a slow terminal keeps clickable paths and the clipboard.**
- **Feat: Health warns when an agent runs an older version than the Agent Store shows.** Writable layers that no version uses are set aside and removed after seven days.

## 2026.10.31.02

**Terminal speed and reliability**

- **Improve: a terminal for a workspace that already runs opens much faster.** On a busy test server the server side of the connect dropped from about 6 seconds to about 0.2 seconds. The **Waking** screen now stays until the terminal shows its first text, so a slow connect no longer looks like a hung black screen.
- **Fix: an install stops with a clear reason when a required program fails to download**, instead of finishing with a terminal that cannot start (thanks to aalencia, GitHub PR #34).

**Script runs (new)**

- **Feat: your scripts can start an agent.** A User Script or a cron job can call `aicli-run` to start a real agent session in a workspace that you can see and use. The script waits for the answer and gets a short report, and the workspace closes when the run ends. A read-only run starts at once. A run that may change files waits for your approval in the Activity tray. You choose which scripts may do this on **Settings, Script runs**.
- **Feat: a script can ask for access.** `aicli-run --request-access` puts a request in the Activity tray and sends one Unraid notification. **Approve** adds the script with the limits it asked for. **Reject** stops it from asking again until the script file changes.
- **Feat: a script approval is a readable card.** It shows the script, the agents, the folders, the mode and the daily limit, with the technical details folded away. Approve and Reject stay in view.
- **Feat: a script can send a follow-up to its open run.** A second call with the same key sends its prompt into the read-only run that is still open, instead of starting a second run.
- **Feat: a run can have its own temporary folder.** `aicli-run --temp` gives the run a private folder on your appdata pool. The plugin removes it a day after the run ends.

**Agents and workspaces**

- **Feat: OpenCode 2 is a new agent in the Agent Store.** It runs beside OpenCode, keeps its own data, and takes your Config Hub choices from OpenCode at its first install.
- **Feat: an agent can start a helper workspace for a task**, report back and close it. This is off until you turn it on in **Settings, Sub-agent workspaces**. An agent can also start an existing workspace.
- **Feat: a workspace can hold several scheduled Continues**, each with an optional reason.
- **Fix: closing a workspace lets the agent save and exit cleanly** instead of a hard stop.
- **Fix: after a reboot every auto-started workspace gets its terminal.** A workspace whose folder was deleted now says so.
- **Fix: when an agent does not take the continue message after a restart**, the plugin presses Enter again, and the Activity tray asks you to press Enter if it stays.
- **Fix: OpenCode sees each plugin skill once**, so new sessions with a local model start much faster. Codex no longer warns at every start that it cannot create its helper commands.
- **Fix: the drawer nests every workspace an agent made under that agent**, and the tab of a deleted workspace closes.
- **Fix: after a restart, an agent gets the continue message once**, also when several pages are open.
- **Fix: the plugin no longer starts its background service again while the server shuts down.**
- **Fix: an agent no longer runs an old version that an earlier install left behind** while the Agent Store shows the new one.

**Agent Store and upgrades**

- **Feat: an Agent Store card shows the version you run and the new version in full.** Select the new version to see its release notes and what an update does. The card also says how much space **Remove old versions** and **Uninstall** free, and **Check for updates** shows its progress.
- **Fix: agent upgrades show real progress, pack about three times faster and survive a server restart.** An upgrade no longer waits for a home save that is not needed, or for old versions that no workspace uses.
- **Fix: the Beta version list shows only the newest builds** and hides builds older than the stable release.
- **Fix: Remove old versions finds every old version**, and a damaged cached install file is downloaded again.
- **Fix: an Agent Store card on a phone keeps its height while an agent installs.**

**Settings and Activity tray**

- **Feat: the Settings page is easier to use.** It has plain labels, an (i) next to each setting for its help, cards that you can fold and reorder, Advanced parts that stay closed, and a Storage tab built from cards. A storage change waits for an **Apply** button.
- **Feat: the Activity tray shows who acted**, for example "by root (John)", with an optional display name in Settings. Rows that offer only Dismiss leave after 5 minutes.
- **Fix: a plugin page whose Unraid sign-in ended stops asking the server for updates** and shows a **Sign in again** bar, so it no longer blocks your next sign-in.

**Notebook**

- **Feat: voice mail notes have their own Voice mail heading**, folded at first, with a count of new messages.
- **Improve: the Notebook opens faster**, also with many notes or a large note. The button that asks the agent to refresh a note is always in the note header.
- **Fix: the file editor no longer replaces a note that an agent changed while you edited it.** It keeps your text, says who changed the note, and offers Reload and Copy my text.
- **Fix: the Notebook and the Secrets folder work on an iPhone**, and the Notebook is easier to use with a screen reader, a keyboard, a finger and low vision.

**Storage and boot disk**

- **Feat: the Boot disk space card can archive and restore old layer images and old session logs.** It warns at 80 % full and refuses large writes over 85 % full. Your saves are never held back.
- **Feat: a home card shows the old layers kept after Convert to plain folders**, with their size, the date they are removed, and a **Remove old layers** button. Configuration shows **Home storage** and **Agent storage** separately.
- **Fix: an array stop with plugin storage on a pool no longer leaves the pool busy** (thanks to Joly0, GitHub PR #30). **Up one level** in the folder picker works again (thanks to Joly0, GitHub PR #32).
- **Fix: a change of the home storage folder moves each home safely**, so home mounts no longer fail and the system log no longer fills (GitHub #33).
- **Fix: saving home changes no longer removes files from a home that is in use** (GitHub #21, #9).

**Config Hub and Relay**

- **Security: a secret that you typed by hand into a Codex, Grok Build or Goose block no longer shows in the Config drift view.**
- **Feat: the Config drift card is easier to read.** It has plain state words, a hover text on each button, and a **Compare** window that shows both texts side by side.
- **Fix: Release on the Codex "command environment" row no longer removes Codex from every MCP server.** Global Instructions shows Claude Code and OpenCode as covered when they already read your instructions.
- **Fix: the workspace config tree offers the right project file.** For OpenCode it is opencode.json in the project folder. **+ Add** opens an empty file even when its folder does not exist yet, and a file that two rows link to shows once.
- **Improve: the Relay command has help for every action**, and an empty inbox says how to see messages that you already read.

## 2026.10.21.01

**Live dictation (new)**

- **Feat: see your words while you speak.** The new setting **Live transcription endpoint** (Settings, Agent voice) takes the address of a streaming transcription engine. The page then sends your voice to the engine as you talk. It types each word while you speak and corrects the words as the engine hears more. A pause ends the sentence. A **Test** button next to the setting checks the connection.
- **Feat: dictation goes on when the live engine is not available.** If the live engine cannot be reached, dictation uses the transcription endpoint, or your browser's own recognition if that is not set, and it says so.
- **Improve: the Settings dictation Test shows the words while you speak.** When a live endpoint is set, **Test (records 3 s, 8 s live)** streams for 8 seconds and shows the words as you say them.
- **Fix: dictation with a transcription engine no longer types labels such as "[BLANK_AUDIO]"** for a pause or a silent piece.

**Storage**

- **Fix: changes of the Persistence engine are safer.** Before a change starts, the plugin checks that the storage has enough free space. It refuses to start while installs, backups or moves run. If a conversion fails, the plugin puts every item back, keeps your data, and the Settings page names the item and the cause. The engine selector on the Configuration tab keeps your choice while the warning is open, and **Cancel** puts back the engine in use.
- **Fix: Convert to plain folders is no longer refused because of a left-over empty marker file.** When it is refused, the Activity tray names the folder and the first file in the way, and says that nothing was changed.

**Reliability and safety**

- **Fix: a large reliability and safety update from a full review of the plugin.** More than 180 defects are fixed. Saving, merging, backing up and converting homes no longer report success when nothing was saved. A save that waits for another save now says so instead of failing. Two saves of the same home at the same time no longer wait for 30 seconds; the second one skips, because the first one saves the same changes.
- **Fix: a home card says again what a running job does** (for example "to save" or "to merge").
- **Fix: converting agents to plain folders keeps the agents you selected** and always shows its result.
- **Fix: a failed request shows its reason**, not a dialog that waits for ever. Many smaller web page defects are fixed.
- **Fix: agent installs, upgrades and shutdowns are safer.** A failed reinstall puts the old version back. A native agent gets the same time to save its work at shutdown as other agents.
- **Fix: file paths with control characters are refused.**

**Terminal and agents**

- **Fix: the terminal page no longer keeps the browser busy.** On a busy page, Chrome could show "Page Unresponsive". The page now reacts to a resize only when the size of the terminal changed.
- **Fix: a new agent workspace starts again after a storage conversion** left the agent attached to a folder that was later removed.
- **Fix: the Relay command of an agent works when the agent puts it in quotes.**
- **Improve: the plugin recognises Claude's weekly limit message** and shows when the limit resets.

## 2026.10.17.02

**Boot disk space (new)**

- **Feat: see where the boot disk space goes.** The Home Storage tab has a **Boot disk space** card. It shows how much each agent, each old agent version and each home uses, with the time of the measurement and a **Measure now** button, and it puts the action that helps next to each line. The boot-disk warning now names the part that is full and points to the card.
- **Feat: remove old agent versions.** **Remove old versions** in the Agent Store card frees the space of agent versions that no workspace uses. The new setting **Keep the previous version for rollback** (on by default) decides whether each agent keeps its last version.
- **Feat: new agents use plain folders on an internal boot disk.** When the server boots from an internal disk, not a USB stick, a new agent is installed as plain folders. An agent kept in layers can be converted.
- **Feat: caches of a plain-folder home stay off the boot disk.** **Cache location for plain-folder homes** keeps the download caches of tools such as npm and pip in RAM (the default) or in a folder on a pool. **Clear caches** empties them while no workspace of that home runs.
- **Feat: move old conversations out of the home.** **Move old sessions…** moves old agent conversation history to a folder on a pool, and **Bring back…** returns it.

**Storage safety (thanks to Marcin M on the forum)**

- **Fix: "Writable layer for homes = Disk" now completes on a home that has Claude Code conversations.** The move waited for ever, because the clean-up after a save kept every conversation file in RAM. A file the save has captured can now go. When a move cannot happen, the message says why.
- **Fix: one damaged saved layer no longer stops the whole home.** A damaged newest layer of a home is moved to a `.bad` folder (never deleted), the home starts without it, and an Unraid notice names the layer. Any other layer that will not mount stops the home with the layer and the reason named.
- **Fix: a damaged or missing layer list is restored, not overwritten.** The plugin keeps a backup of its list of saved layers and rebuilds the list from the layers on disk when needed. A home whose layers exist but whose list entry is missing is recorded again.
- **Fix: a save with nothing to save says "Nothing to save"**, not a green "Persisted", in the dialog and in the Activity tray. A save in an Emergency Session says **Not saved**.
- **Fix: the Emergency Session says that work done in it is lost**, next to the **Start Emergency Session** button and inside the session, also after a page reload.
- **Fix: a busy home whose writable layer is on disk is no longer asked to save every few seconds.** Its changes are already on the disk; the home card now says they go into a layer when the home is idle.

**Upgrades and the Activity tray**

- **Fix: a long agent upgrade no longer shows "stalled".** While the new version is written to the boot disk, the Activity tray stays alive and shows the percent done.

**Workspaces and the array**

- **Fix: workspaces on the array or a pool no longer try to start while the array stops**, so the array can stop. They start again when the array is back.

**Voice and the Notebook**

- **Fix: the Notebook works for agents with the Notebook switch alone.** Plugin management no longer needs to be on.
- **Improve: dictation goes on with your browser's own recognition when the speech server is down**, and says so. The Settings dictation **Test** still tests the server itself.
- **Fix: the microphone icon stops pulsing as soon as you stop dictation.**
- **Fix: a dictation request that is refused now leaves a line in the log and in the voice status**, so the reason can be found.

**Settings and backups**

- **Fix: the scheduled home backup now runs.** It failed every time, and nothing said so; a failed scheduled backup is now written to the log.
- **New setting: Keep the terminal responsive** (off by default). It gives the Unraid web page and the terminals a higher priority than other programs, so typing stays quick while the server is busy.
- **New setting: Agent temporary folder.** Agents can keep their temporary files in RAM (the default), in a folder on a pool, or on an internal boot disk.
- **Fix: the storage picker offers a folder inside each pool, user share, array disk and Unassigned Devices drive**, not its top folder, and a new save of a top folder is refused with the reason.

**Smaller fixes**

- **Fix: the "Could not create folder" message in the folder picker stays until you close it.**
- **Fix: on a sidebar theme, the home backup dialog no longer sits under the side menu on a phone.**
- **Improve: a file path in the terminal is a link only when the file exists**, checked when the mouse is over the line.
- **Fix: the Relay contact list no longer shows closed or repeated workspaces.**
- **Fix: RESET on a workspace's Details card starts a new conversation, as its text says.**
- **Fix: the Relay notice preview shows the wording of the newest choice**, and the Config Hub line for no installed agents is easy to read.
- **Docs: the first-run guide, the help texts of the Relay, Plugin management and Config Hub tabs, and the README describe the plugin as it is now.**

## 2026.10.15.03

&gt; **The plugin is now open source under the MIT license.** The `LICENSE` file is at the top of the repository, and the licenses of the bundled libraries are in `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`. The public history now shows each change as its own commit, and `CONTRIBUTING.md` says how a pull request is handled. The Notebook hang warning from 2026.10.13.01 still applies: if an Unraid page hangs with the Notebook on, set **Notebook** to Off on the Configuration tab and tell us on GitHub.

**Config Hub (thanks to Joly0 on GitHub)**

- **Feat: switch an MCP server off for all agents without losing its agent choices.** Each server row has an on/off switch. A server that is off is removed from every agent's config at the next Apply, and comes back with the same agent ticks when you switch it on.
- **Feat: a remote MCP server can log in and send HTTP headers.** Choose **Bearer token** or **Custom header** under Authentication, and add extra headers if the server's docs ask for them. A token is never stored as typed text: keep it under Secrets and type its key in braces, for example `{MY_TOKEN}`. The token fields have the eye icon to show the value.
- **Feat: a Test connection button checks a remote server before you save.** It connects from your Unraid server and shows the HTTP status and a short reason. It saves nothing.
- **Improve: a Config Hub write that fails names its real cause in the log,** such as a broken link to a skills folder.

**Storage**

- **Fix: merging a home's layers works again on Unraid's mksquashfs 4.5** (reported on GitHub). The plugin checks what the installed mksquashfs supports before it asks for progress output. When a merge fails, the log now shows mksquashfs's own error message.
- **Feat: a home kept in layers can be converted to plain folders** from its card on the Storage tab (**Convert to plain folders**). The home then needs no saves, merges or tidy-ups. Every workspace of the home closes and opens again, the Activity tray names each step, and the old layers are kept for 14 days. A conversion that fails rolls back cleanly.
- **Fix: a removed agent layer frees its space on the flash at once,** and storage layers no longer stay attached after they are unmounted.
- **Fix: installing, upgrading or checking agents for updates no longer fills your server's RAM.** npm kept every download in `/root/.npm`, which is in RAM on Unraid, until the next reboot. Each npm run now uses its own cache folder and removes it when it ends.

**Terminals and workspaces**

- **Fix: a terminal start that hangs now ends with an error after a minute** instead of showing Initializing forever (reported on GitHub). Old terminal connections from a dropped browser are cleaned up when a workspace starts.
- **Fix: agent sessions find tools installed in `~/.local/bin`** (reported on GitHub).
- **Fix: a terminal whose connection drops reconnects only when its workspace still exists,** so a workspace closed in another browser no longer shows an error page.
- **Fix: large files upload again,** where they failed with "The server answered with HTML instead of JSON".
- **Fix: a path in the terminal that starts with `/`, `./` or `~/` opens on a click whatever its file type,** for example `~/.claude/secrets/ha.token` or `/etc/ssl/site.crt`. Before, only a fixed list of file types was a link. A path inside a web address, such as `ftp://host/file.x`, is not a link.
- **Fix: a new Grok Build workspace starts Grok fresh** instead of stopping at "No session found for current directory".
- **Fix: the Activity tray's "needs approval" label and its Approve, Force and error texts are easy to read** on light and dark themes.

**Voice**

- **Fix: dictation works with the voice engine again.** Speech is sent in a format every engine accepts, and an engine error stays on screen long enough to read.
- **Fix: the Agent Store header stays inside its card on a phone** when the version-check line is long.

## 2026.10.13.01

&gt; **Known issue: a page can hang while the Notebook is on.** A few Unraid pages have frozen on one server while the Notebook was turned on. We have not found the cause yet. This release makes the Notebook ask the server for much less (see below) and adds a way to record what happens, but we cannot promise it is fixed.
&gt;
&gt; **If an Unraid page hangs or freezes with the Notebook on:** open **Settings, AI CLI Agents, Configuration**, find the **Notebook** card and set **Notebook** to Off. The page frees up at once, and nothing is deleted. Then please open an issue on GitHub (the **Support** menu on the Debug Console tab has a **Create GitHub issue** button) or write on the forum support thread. Tell us what hung (every Unraid page or only the plugin pages), how long it lasted, and what your server was doing. If you can, tick **Performance trace** on the **Debug Console** tab before it happens again, and attach a support bundle.

**Notebook hang watch**

- **Improve: the Notebook asks the server for much less.** The plugin remembers which workspace a note belongs to for 20 seconds, so each check no longer re-tests the home storage mount. A burst of reconnects now causes one refresh, not one refresh for each reconnect. A menu layer that cannot find its anchor stops trying after 120 tries.
- **Feat: a "Performance trace" tick box on the Debug Console tab.** It is off by default, and the plugin writes nothing extra while it is off. When you tick it, the plugin writes one timing line for each step that is slow (a slow request, a slow check of the home mount, a slow Notebook scan, a slow save to the boot drive) and a short WARN line in the Debug log. Untick it when you have finished.
- **Fix: the Activity tray no longer leaves a check running after you leave the page.**

**User guide and the Notebook wiki**

- **Feat: a user guide for the whole plugin, on GitHub.** There is one page for each feature and a reference that lists every setting on every tab. Open the `docs/user-guide` folder of the repository, or follow the link at the top of the README.
- **Feat: the Wiki view builds its contents from the links between pages.** Pages that nothing links to show under "Not linked yet". A note page has a compact header with a Properties panel, the Wiki has a "Recent" popover, and a note can open in its own browser tab.
- **Feat: an optional Wiki page in the Tasks menu.** Turn on "Show the Wiki as its own page" on the Configuration tab to read and edit the wiki without opening a workspace.
- **Feat: a note is limited to 1 MB**, and a masked value in a note has an eye icon to show it.

**Storage you can see and control**

- **Feat: choose where each home keeps what you change between saves:** in RAM (fast, no disk wear, lost on a crash until saved) or on disk (survives a crash or power cut). The new "Writable layer for homes" setting on the Configuration tab shows a clear warning first, then closes your open workspaces, saves each home into a verified layer, mounts it again and checks the result. If a home cannot move, the setting is put back and nothing is deleted. Disk is refused on USB flash.
- **Fix: merging a home's saved layers now frees the space it should.** Before, one small file written during a merge made it keep the whole writable layer, so gigabytes stayed on the flash. Automatic saves of a home in use no longer copy an on-disk writable layer every 30 minutes. Uninstalling an agent now removes every version of it from storage.
- **Improve: Consolidate on a home card now also saves your unsaved changes,** so it works with one layer too. The Repair button shows only when a home is not mounted. A home merge shows named steps and progress, and a storage job that is put off shows as waiting, with the reason.
- **Feat: the Consolidate dialog has a box to skip the automatic Continue.** Untick it and the closed workspaces reopen without a message, so they use no tokens until you tell them to go on.
- **Improve: the storage warning says in plain words what is wrong** and that it comes from AI CLI Agents. It names the home or agent. A leftover entry for a test folder that no longer exists is removed at start-up and no longer raises a warning.
- **Feat: the Health tab warns when deleted layers still pin space on the boot drive** and names the workspaces to restart, and when a writable layer on a filling boot drive is large.
- **Fix: closing a storage warning in any way puts the setting back,** a click outside the warning no longer closes it, and Cancel on the persistence engine dialog no longer risks starting a move.

**Notebook, voice mail and the Activity tray**

- **Feat: voice mail messages are also kept as notes.** With Voice and the Notebook on, each message becomes a note. Deleting it from voice mail leaves the note. You archive and delete it like any note.
- **Feat: the agent is told when you answer in the Notebook:** a question card answered, a checklist finished or failed, a comment, or a login saved. The message names the note and never repeats your answer. A switch in Settings &gt; Notebook turns it off.
- **Feat: delete a note at once.** A bin icon and a Delete item remove a note with an Undo pill for 8 seconds. A note goes to the Archive; a note already in the Archive is removed for good.
- **Feat: a Refresh button on a note asks the open workspace to update it,** and the Notebook line in the Activity tray names the workspace and has an Open note button.
- **Feat: voice mail messages delete at once with an Undo pill.** The Voice section of a workspace menu is always collapsed when the menu opens.
- **Improve: Activity tray notices read in plain words.** The title says what happened, the line under it says who did it or what comes next, a finished record shows its age instead of a Done badge, a failure shows one sentence and the way out, and Cancel appears only where it can stop something.
- **Fix: the spoken voice falls back to English** when the voice you chose is missing.

**Agent Store and the folder picker**

- **Fix: saving an agent's secrets no longer restarts every workspace.** A notice says how many running workspaces still use the old values and offers "Restart them now". Busy workspaces are never restarted by it. The Agent Store also says when versions were last fetched and shows when a check is running or failed.
- **Feat: the folder picker has a breadcrumb, collapsible favourites, a sort choice and a filter.** The current folder in the breadcrumb is easier to read.
- **Improve: the two second rows of a wide Notebook drawer line up,** and the note-list toggle sits level with the tabs.

**Agents that work together and on their own**

- **Improve: Relay costs agents fewer tokens.** An agent's inbox shows only what is new (`inbox --all` shows older messages), and the plugin types one notice for a batch of unread messages, not one per message. This also works on Codex and OpenCode queues. The wait before a new notice is a setting (default 10 minutes). The notice typed into an agent is shorter by default, with presets or your own wording in settings.
- **Fix: auto-continue reads a Codex retry date such as "try again at Oct 14th, 2026 9:49 PM"** and no longer assumes five hours. A usage limit that has lifted, or work that has resumed, clears the old schedule on Codex workspaces.
- **Fix: Codex workspaces resume after a close.** The plugin could save a command flag as the conversation id; ids now come from the agent's own session files.
- **Fix: closing a workspace no longer stops a system service an agent started.**
- **Improve: long workspace names scroll once when you hover the row.**

## 2026.10.06.02

**The Notebook (new)**

- **Feat: a Notebook drawer where agents leave organised notes for you.** It opens beside the terminal and holds pages you can read, checklists and test scripts you can tick, diagrams, forms where an agent asks you a question, a linked wiki, and the logins for the app under test. The notes are plain files in a `notebook` folder in each project, kept in git. It is on by default; Settings &gt; Notebook has its own card and an on/off switch.
- **Feat: the speaker button reads the whole note aloud.** A ring shows while the voice is made, a moving wave shows while it plays, and a second click pauses and then continues. A note being read and a message from a workspace take turns and never talk over each other.
- **Feat: a file path in backticks in a note opens that file,** the same way a path in the terminal does. When the Notebook is pinned, a Wiki button sits in the row of icons at the top and turns into a note button while the wiki is open.
- **Fix: a Notebook page opens with its scripts off** and a Run scripts button, so a page that loops can no longer freeze the tab.
- **Feat: agents are told about voice and the Notebook** in their instruction file, but only while each is switched on. An agent picks a spoken name from its workspace name and its own voice, and can fetch one exact Relay message.

**Workspaces and the drawer**

- **Improve: long workspace names run as a ticker.** On a desktop drawer a name that is cut off moves left at a steady pace and loops by itself, and pauses while you hover the row. With reduce-motion on it stays still. On a phone the name wraps onto two lines, and pressing and holding a row opens a Details sheet that fits the screen. The old card ran off the edge. The labels in it are easier to read.
- **Fix: reloading the page returns to the workspace that tab showed,** the page no longer drops back to another workspace when one list is missing yours, and a Go to link for a workspace that is gone now says so.
- **Fix: one image paste makes one file.** A file path that wraps onto a second terminal line is one clickable link.
- **Fix: Reload on a Codex workspace finds its conversation** instead of refusing, and the automatic continue now works for Codex's "Selected model is at capacity" message even though Codex prints its own recap under it.

**Reliability**

- **Fix: saving your home no longer fails when the boot disk is nearly full.** It copies only the databases that are in use, a blocked save warns you and shows in the tray, and the plugin warns you at 85 percent full and says what uses the space. A plugin update now waits for a running save instead of stopping it, so it no longer leaves a duplicate 1 GB layer.
- **Fix: every agent's databases are checked and repaired when it starts.** A damaged one is rebuilt, or moved aside and never deleted, so the agent loads after a hard stop. A database another process holds open is left alone.
- **Improve: a Relay message held because Claude's task list is showing says so** in the Activity tray, instead of "a menu was open".
- **Fix: a Relay message to Claude is submitted even when the terminal was scrolled,** and a Relay workspace that cannot start raises an alert and a spoken notice.
- **Improve: the log says when a workspace's tmux session ends,** and the system log survives a reboot, so a lost session can be explained.
- **Fix: Unraid no longer writes "Invalid .page format" to the system log on every page.**

## 2026.10.01.04

**Voice**

- **Feat: set up local dictation from Settings.** Settings &gt; Agent voice has a Set up local dictation button. It installs a Whisper transcription server (Speaches) and connects it. If the server runs but has no model, Connect downloads the Whisper model by itself and shows how long it has been going. Both voice setup rows show a four-step list: container running, server answers, model ready, settings saved. An installed voice container shows a Connect button, its state and its last log line.
- **Improve: the dictation Test button shows what is happening.** It counts down the seconds, shows your words as you speak, says "Transcribing…" while the server works, gives up with a message after 60 seconds, and shows the real error when the transcription fails.
- **Improve: the Activity tray entry for a spoken message names the workspace, shows the first words that were said, and says whether it was played or kept as voice mail.**

**Workspaces and files**

- **Fix: your workspace order in the drawer stays put after an update.** A reorder is saved at once and is no longer lost.
- **Fix: a new workspace no longer loads its terminal before it is ready.**
- **Feat: files under /tmp (agent scratch files) open in the viewer, read-only.**
- **Fix: a stuck Relay notice now wakes the agent** and logs what the agent was doing.
- **Fix: a storage rebuild also clears a home that runs on disk.**

## 2026.09.30.04

**Agents that keep working on their own**

- **Feat: a workspace continues by itself after a temporary model error.** When a provider is overloaded, rate-limits you or drops the connection, the plugin waits 1, 5 and then 15 minutes and tells the agent to continue. After three tries the Activity tray asks you to look. It only types when the agent is idle at its prompt. Turn it off or change the waits in Settings.
- **Feat: schedule a Continue for any workspace.** The workspace menu has Continue now and Schedule, with an optional daily or weekly repeat. A small clock next to the workspace name shows the schedule; click it to change or cancel it. When Claude Code or Codex reports a usage limit, the plugin schedules the Continue for the reset time by itself. An agent can also schedule one with its plugin tools.

- **Feat: your own auto-continue patterns.** Settings has a new Auto-continue patterns section. See the built-in screen patterns for each agent, and add, edit, switch off or delete your own for a model error, a usage limit with a retry time, a busy marker or a status line. Each pattern must match a sample and is checked for safety before it is saved, and "Test against a workspace screen" shows which lines match. After a save you can report a pattern: a preview with secrets masked opens a prefilled GitHub issue that you submit with your own login. Agents with plugin tools can read a workspace's screen (plain text, secrets masked, every read logged) and propose a pattern for you to approve.
- **Fix: auto-continue recognises the OpenCode and Kilo message "usage exceeded … retry in 1h 21m"** and continues after the stated wait.

**Voice (new and improved)**

- **Feat: set up the natural voice from Settings.** Settings &gt; Agent voice has a Set up natural voice button. It checks that Docker runs, prepares the Kokoro template, opens Unraid's own Add Container page for you to apply, and then connects to the voice engine by itself.
- **Fix: the natural voice setup works on the default settings.** The voice engine container no longer stops at once with "Permission denied"; it uses the voice model inside its image. If an engine made by an earlier test version stops with that error, remove its Model cache path in the container settings.
- **Fix: the dictation Test button in Settings shows what you said** instead of always "Nothing was recognised".
- **Improve: dictation on a phone is a small bar above the terminal's key row** instead of a bubble over the terminal output. It has a Stop/Close button (Escape works too) and an Enter button that stops listening, types the last words and presses Enter without opening the keyboard. Closing frees the microphone, and the phone keyboard opens again on the next tap.
- **Feat: "Send when I stop talking".** When it is on, two seconds of silence after you speak ends the dictation and presses Enter. It replaces "Send on stop" and keeps your choice.
- **Fix: dictation presses Enter reliably.** "Send on stop" never pressed Enter in Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode or Kilo, because the dictated words looked like typing in progress; Enter is still held when a menu or a question is on screen, and the notice about it now also shows after you close the bar. The last phrase is no longer typed twice, and dictation from the iPhone keyboard's own microphone no longer types every guess again.
- **Fix: a workspace set to voice mail stays silent.** When an agent named its workspace by the display name instead of its id, the message played aloud and was kept apart from the workspace's other voice mail.
- **Feat: you hear which workspace speaks.** Each message starts with a short "&lt;name&gt; says:", live and when you play it later. Give a workspace a spoken name (workspace menu &gt; Voice &gt; Spoken name) when its display name reads badly aloud.
- **Improve: stop a message with one click.** While a workspace speaks, its play button shows a moving voice wave; click it to stop at once. The unheard count shows up to 99 (then 99+) instead of 9+.
- **Feat: a different voice for each workspace.** The voice on the Settings page stays the default; choose another one for a workspace in its menu (Voice &gt; Voice…), with a Test button. The Spoken name dialog has a Test button too. Switching voice on now says "Voice enabled."

**Linked boxes (new)**

- **Feat: workspaces on two Unraid boxes can message each other.** Pair two boxes once with a one-time code in Settings &gt; Agent Relay. Workspaces on the other box then appear as contacts (for example "mvp-dmoe @ tower"), messages arrive like local ones, wait while the other box is offline, and replies go back to the right workspace. Nothing is shared until you turn it on and pair; both boxes need this version.

**Unraid sidebar themes**

- **Fix: the plugin now fits Unraid's sidebar themes (Azure and Gray, with the menu down the left side).** The terminal, the workspace drawer and the pop-ups now start beside the menu instead of underneath it; the Top-menu themes look the same as before. On the sidebar themes the menu shows the plugin's logo instead of cut-off text, and a menu label you hover shows over the workspace drawer.
- **Improve: the plugin's buttons look like Unraid's own buttons** in every theme (white, black, azure and gray), for example in Settings, the Agent Store and the workspace drawer. Their text is a shade stronger than Unraid's own so it is easy to read, and all text in the drawer and on the Settings page meets the readability standard in every theme.

**Phones and tablets**

- **Improve: the terminal works properly with touch.** A one-finger swipe scrolls back through the session history with momentum, and the page no longer pulls to refresh. A key row under the terminal adds Esc, Tab, Ctrl-C, the arrow keys, Paste and Select. Tap and hold for a Paste / Select menu; Select shows the history as plain text for normal phone selection and Copy. The terminal stays above the on-screen keyboard while you type.
- **Improve: every Settings tab fits a phone.** Configuration, Agent Store, Home Storage, Config Hub, Agent Relay and the Debug Console no longer run past the screen edge: card headers wrap, row buttons sit under their row, labels sit above full-width fields, the tab bar shows whole labels, and every control is large enough to tap, with field text that does not make iOS zoom in.
- **Improve: on a phone the workspace drawer's pull tab is short** (workspace list, microphone and a More button), so it no longer covers the start of the terminal lines. More shows the other actions for five seconds. The tab never covers Unraid's header.
- **Fix: a phone swipe scrolls back through Codex output again** (Codex 0.158 started in full-screen mode; the plugin now starts it inline).
- **Improve: every dialog, menu and panel fits a phone.** Buttons are large enough to tap, nothing runs off the screen, text is easier to read, and the file editor keeps its tools on one row. Confirm dialogs such as "Discard changes?" now open on top of the editor and the drawer instead of behind them.
- **Fix: pasting an image from the Paste button works on iPhone and iPad** in Safari and Chrome. Tap Paste, then the Paste bubble iOS shows. A small preview of a pasted image now appears briefly so you can see the right picture reached the agent.
- **Fix: a swipe on OpenCode on a touch screen scrolls the conversation** instead of moving its cursor (seen on a Windows tablet), and tapping Latest after a fast swipe always returns to the live screen.
- **Fix: with the terminal page open on two computers, each keeps the workspace you chose on it.** Before, a click on one could switch the other a few seconds later.
- **Fix: opening the terminal page on a phone or a second browser no longer shrinks the terminals of all your workspaces.** Only the workspaces you open there are resized.

**Agent installs and upgrades**

- **Fix: after an upgrade or downgrade, new workspaces run the version the Store shows.** Some agents kept running the old version, or recorded the wrong one, and GitHub Copilot could run its own newer cached copy. An upgrade whose files cannot be saved now fails and keeps the current version instead of reporting success.
- **Fix: opening a workspace a few seconds after an agent install no longer shows Agent Binary Missing.** The plugin now waits briefly while its storage check holds the agent, instead of giving up.
- **Fix: an agent is never replaced by an empty package** (reported on the Unraid forum for Antigravity CLI: "Agent Binary Missing" after every update). An install, update, storage move or storage engine switch packed a link to the agent's folder instead of the folder itself; it now always packs the real folder, and an empty package is refused. An agent with nothing stored no longer shows as installed.
- **Improve: upgrades beside running workspaces cover more agents and explain themselves.** Grok Build, Kimi Code and Antigravity CLI keep their sign-in in one place shared by every version. Switching a workspace to the new version reconnects its terminal in place instead of reloading the page, open terminals stay usable during an upgrade, and a queued upgrade can be cancelled. The Store counts every running workspace, also those with no browser open.
- **Improve: agents installed as plain folders (such as Grok Build, Kimi Code, Codex and Antigravity CLI) now upgrade side by side, also while their workspaces run.** A new workspace gets the new version at once, running workspaces keep theirs and offer "Switch to the installed version", and your sign-in is shared by every version. A failed switch-over waits longer between tries and stops after six instead of retrying every few seconds. Older versions are now removed from the flash drive: the plugin keeps the current and the previous version, and any version a workspace still uses. Uninstalling an agent now also removes its kept versions, and restoring an older version no longer damages the current one.
- **Fix: agent updates no longer fill the USB flash drive.** Each new agent version is now stored as one fresh copy instead of another layer on top of all the old ones, and old copies that nothing uses are removed (the current and the previous version are kept). Agents that already piled up layers are tidied once when they are idle. An install that would not fit on the flash drive is refused with a clear reason instead of failing half-way.
- **Fix: an agent install no longer fails when the vendor's server sends its install script compressed** (seen with Antigravity CLI), and a failed install now says whether the vendor or a full flash drive was the cause.
- **Fix: release channels keep the Stable, Beta or pinned setting you chose**, and the version picker lists every available version.
- **Fix: the install progress window no longer appears to stop at the tmux step.**

**Home backups**

- **Fix: home backup settings now save.** Before, a change to the backup folder, mode, how many backups to keep, the schedule or the other options showed "Saved" but was not kept. Each home now has its own backup settings behind a **Backup…** button on its card on the Storage page. Pick the folder with the normal folder browser, which can now also create a new folder; every change saves at once and stays after a reload. Each backup can now be deleted as well as restored, and when earlier backups are found but no folder is set, the dialog offers that folder with one click. The card shows when the home was last backed up, and a running backup shows its progress there. A home keeps the settings you had before until you change them.
- **Fix: a warm home backup no longer fails at "Verifying the copy" while agents run.** Files that change during the copy count as live changes and the card shows how many; a backup fails only when an unchanged file differs, and the Debug Console log then lists the files. A database that changed during the copy is copied again safely.

**Storage and stability**

- **Fix: on Unraid 7.3.2, saving a home takes a clean copy of each database again.** The database backup silently did nothing, so a save could store a live database file mid-write, and merging a home's saved layers failed.
- **Fix: a home whose storage place changed while it was open is saved again.** After an upgrade on a pool or a non-USB boot device, a save of such a home could read an empty folder, save nothing and still report success. Each save and the shutdown save now use the folder the open home really uses, a remount never covers unsaved changes, and the home moves to the new place by itself when no session uses it.
- **Fix: saving a home with large agent databases no longer fills the server's memory.** The copies of the databases now go to the same drive as the home's changes, only when it has room, and are always removed when the save ends. A save that cannot complete waits before the next automatic try (2 minutes, growing to 30 minutes) instead of trying again every few seconds. A home that is always in use can be saved again while its agents run.
- **Fix: storage moves are safer.** Before you move agent or home storage to a /mnt/user share, the plugin explains the risk (heavy writes through Unraid's shared-folder layer can freeze the server) and suggests better places; /mnt/user stays allowed when you have no other choice, and a share that lives on one pool is used directly. A storage move no longer closes Unraid's own web terminal or other plugins' terminals.
- **Fix: new workspaces no longer run agent work through /mnt/user by default, and the folder browser no longer scans large shares in full**, both of which could slow the whole server.
- **Improve: the Storage page shows what is saved and what is not.** Unsaved changes have their own tile, a running save or merge shows on the home card and locks its buttons, and the figures are correct on disk and flash pools. One global storage setting now applies to every home.
- **Fix: saving and merging homes is more reliable.** Memory held by an old copy is released after a merge, a queued save no longer gets stuck, a closed session comes back after a merge, a second OpenCode workspace no longer fails with a missing cache folder during a save, and a noisy kernel warning at every refresh is gone.
- **Fix: a reboot with many workspaces no longer hangs**, because the plugin always keeps time to release its storage mounts at shutdown. After a reboot, a workspace opened before the array started now opens by itself once the array is up.
- **Fix: Persist, a backup or an agent install no longer reports "saved" when nothing was saved.** A save that meets the plugin's own storage check waits for it and then saves, or says it did not save.
- **New: an agent, or you from a shell, can save or merge a home without the WebUI** (the persist-home and consolidate-home commands and tools; a merge waits for your approval in the Activity tray).

**Agent Relay**

- **Feat: let a trusted external system send requests to named topics.** On a remote's row in Settings &gt; Agent Relay, the new Permissions button lets you allow that remote to send requests to the topics you choose and to follow their progress; nothing is allowed until you turn it on. A remote can cancel its own open requests when you also allow cancel, repeated requests with the same client id are recognised, and removing a permission cancels that remote's open requests. Every grant change and request is recorded.
- **Fix: a request to an archived topic is refused, and a topic actor is reminded of a request it acknowledged but has not finished.**
- **Security: the Relay no longer opens a network listener or creates a key until you turn it on**, and it no longer keeps running old plugin code after an update. A listener left behind by an older plugin version is now found and stopped, even when the listener is switched off.
- **Fix: updating the plugin no longer hangs** when the Relay listener is switched on, and the listener starts again by itself if it stops.
- **Fix: after an update, agents' Relay and admin tools use the new plugin code without a workspace restart.** (A workspace started before this version needs one restart for this to take effect.)
- **Fix: a message to a linked box is sent at once when that box is online**, instead of waiting for the next automatic send, and the contact list no longer shows test workspaces or long-closed sessions.
- **Fix: Relay messages to an idle OpenCode workspace are no longer held back** by the grey hint text in its input box.
- **Fix: a Relay notice that was typed into an agent's input box but not sent is now finished automatically** within a few seconds, also in OpenCode. If it still does not go, the plugin stops after three tries and shows one Activity item, instead of pressing Enter again and again; it reads only the real input box and never presses Enter over your own typing, and other Relay messages are no longer held back behind it. The Activity tray no longer calls it an open menu, and its button now just presses Enter instead of typing the notice a second time.

**Workspaces and terminals**

- **Improve: switching between workspaces is fast, also right after a plugin update.** Open terminals no longer drop when the plugin updates: a terminal connection is renewed only when its own code changed. The plugin reconnects every running workspace's terminal in the background, and on a desktop the terminal page keeps up to 10 of them ready while hidden, so a switch shows the live terminal at once instead of after two to three seconds. Nothing is started or typed by this; a phone keeps only the open terminal.
- **Fix: "Switch to the installed version" does what it says.** It starts the agent once, not twice, and sends no Continue when it says it will not. A Continue or Relay notice is never typed into a workspace before its agent has drawn its screen, and a Continue whose Enter did not take is no longer reported as sent.
- **Feat: the drawer shows unreachable copies of a workspace's agent** (for example after a double start), with Show screen (read only) and Stop this copy; the visible workspace keeps running.
- **Improve: the Debug Console header is one compact row** with the log tabs, filters, icon buttons and a Support menu for the support bundle, forum post, GitHub issue and known issues, so the log shows more lines.

**Other fixes and improvements**

- **Security: a workspace agent no longer shows its secrets on the process command line**, where any local user could read them.
- **Fix: OpenCode follows your Claude global instructions and rule files again.**
- **Fix: a workspace continues by itself again after a model error whose message wrapped over two lines** (seen with an NVIDIA overload in a narrow terminal).
- **Improve: the Store and the workspace list respond faster when many terminals are open.**
- **Fix: on a phone, the open Activity panel is no longer partly covered by the workspace drawer's buttons.**
- **Improve: the storage maintenance notice can be minimised to a small chip and no longer covers the terminal; on a phone the Activity pill shrinks to a dot and a count and sits above the terminal's key row, and Unraid's scroll arrows no longer cover the Select key.**
- **Fix: on a phone, the drawer's pull tab can no longer be dragged up onto Unraid's header.**
- **Fix: the Activity pill no longer sits on top of the Relay Permissions and storage halt dialogs, so their buttons can be tapped**, and the Running label in a workspace's details is easier to read on the white theme.
- **Fix: on a phone, the Create button in the new-folder box of the workspace picker no longer stays greyed out** after you type a name.
- **Fix: the first-run setup and the terminal page load reliably**, and Unraid's own top-bar Terminal button works on the plugin's page again (the page now keeps one live connection instead of up to eight).
- **Fix: clicking a file path in the terminal opens the file in the editor again**, and the plugin's built-in "write clickable file paths" rule restores itself if its file is lost; it now also covers files outside the workspace.
- **Fix: after the plugin updates itself, a terminal no longer shrinks to a small box.**
- **Fix: a shell an agent opens (or the SSH quick-connect) keeps the workspace folder and the agent's tools.**
- **Fix: the Config Hub's optional settings backup works again.**
- **Fix: the file editor's Close button stays in the top-right corner on a desktop screen.**
- **Improve: the workspace menu is shorter, voice mail plays unheard messages oldest first, and the Unattached sessions list reads more clearly.**
- **Fix: the Agent Store opens on All on a first install**, also when this browser saved another filter earlier.
- **Fix: old agent versions are also removed from the flash drive after the storage engine was switched to layers** (the current and the previous version are kept).
- **Improve: screen readers read the workspace drawer's list as a proper list.**
- **Fix: a page or action no longer fails with an error at the moment the plugin updates.** Each process keeps using one version of the plugin code, and an update no longer removes code that a running process still uses.

## 2026.09.15.08

**Agent Relay — agents that coordinate with each other (new)**

- **Feat: agents can now message each other to coordinate on shared work.** Turn on Agent Relay in Settings and any two workspaces — even two different AI tools working on the same project — can send each other direct messages and coordinate through named topics with an assigned owner. The Relay tab keeps a full, searchable message history, and delivery is reliable: a message is never silently lost, is never pasted into the middle of something you're typing, and a message that has to wait shows in the Activity tray with a button to deliver it by hand.
- **Feat: connect outside machines to the Relay.** Settings &gt; Agent Relay has a Remotes table — add any number of external machines or agents by name, each with its own token you can copy, rotate or remove, and see when it last connected.

**Agent updates no longer interrupt your work**

- **Feat: updating an agent no longer closes or waits for your open workspaces.** The new version installs alongside the one you're already using, so open terminals and conversations carry on untouched while the update completes. Move a workspace onto the new version yourself, whenever you're ready, from its menu — it resumes the same conversation and tells you what it costs first. Three agents that keep their sign-in inside their own install folder (Antigravity, Grok Build and Kimi Code) still have to wait for their sessions to close; while any upgrade is queued, blocked, or waiting on a save, the Store card and Activity tray now explain exactly what is happening and why, instead of looking stuck or reporting a false failure.

**Agent voice — an agent that can speak, listen, and leave you messages (new)**

- **Feat: an agent can now speak a short notice to you.** Turn on Voice in the terminal header or Settings, and an agent tells you when it needs you or has finished — using your browser's own voice, or a text-to-speech server you point it at for real speech on every device. One switch turns voice on or off for all your devices at once, with a mute per workspace.
- **Feat: voice input lets you dictate to an agent.** Tap the microphone (or press Ctrl+Shift+M) to talk instead of type, with spoken commands for Enter, punctuation and more.
- **Feat: voice mail keeps every spoken message so you never miss one.** A workspace shows how many messages you haven't heard yet; play the newest with one click, or open the full voice mail panel. Each message has a delete button, and you can clear everything for one workspace or for all of them — both ask first.

**Workspace favourites (new)**

- **Feat: save a workspace's setup and reopen it in one click.** Add a workspace to favourites from its menu, and after you close it, bring it straight back from the Select Workspace picker or an empty drawer — its agent, folder, launch arguments, environment and secrets all come back automatically.

**Home backup and restore (new)**

- **Feat: back up an agent's home to a target of your choice.** Settings &gt; Storage has a Home backup card: pick a disk or pool, choose a cold or warm backup, how many snapshots to keep and a schedule. A backup verifies itself and brings your sessions back exactly where you left them.
- **Feat: restore a home from any snapshot.** Choose to replace the home entirely or merge the snapshot over what's there; the plugin takes a safety copy of the current state first, so a restore can always be undone.

**Reliability — sessions, terminals and resuming conversations**

- **Fix: closing one workspace no longer disturbs any other running workspace.** Each session now runs its own terminal connection, so shutting one down can no longer take others with it.
- **Fix: you can now open the same workspace on two devices at once** — for example your phone and your desktop — without them repeatedly disconnecting each other; both stay live and mirror each other.
- **Fix: two workspaces open on the same project folder no longer resume each other's conversation.** Each workspace now keeps its own conversation, even when they share a folder.
- **Fix: reopening a named Claude Code workspace resumes the right conversation directly**, instead of popping up Claude's own picker asking you to choose between several sessions that share the same name.
- **Fix: OpenCode and Kilo Code now reliably pick up your previous conversation after a restart**, and opening the same OpenCode workspace twice at once can no longer corrupt its chat history.
- **Improve: your open tabs and terminals reconnect themselves automatically after a plugin update** — no more clicking Reconnect on every workspace by hand.

**Uploads, the file editor and the workspace picker**

- **Fix: a file you drag-and-drop or paste into a workspace now always saves into that workspace**, instead of occasionally landing in the wrong place.
- **Feat: upload several files at once, with progress and automatic path copying.** Every saved file's path is copied to your clipboard (or pasted to the agent) as soon as the upload finishes, and large files now upload in chunks instead of failing outright.
- **Improve: the Select Workspace picker is clearer and fully keyboard-friendly**, scales cleanly to your window size, and creating a new folder steps straight into it.
- **Improve: the built-in file editor can now open dotfiles like `.env`, and files under an agent's own home folder**, plus a "Copy file contents" button; a web address an agent prints in the terminal is now a clickable link.

**Agents that can manage the plugin for you (new)**

- **Feat: turn on Plugin management and an agent can answer questions about the plugin itself** — your workspaces, which agents are installed, storage health, current settings — entirely read-only, with secret values never shown.
- **Feat: an agent can also make routine changes for you**, such as creating or renaming a workspace or changing its settings, and every change is logged in the Activity tray. For anything higher-risk — deleting a workspace, upgrading an agent — it can only propose the change; you approve or reject it yourself.

**Other improvements**

- **Fix: the plugin no longer edits your own `CLAUDE.md` file.** Its guidance for Claude now lives in separate files that Claude reads on its own, so your personal instructions file stays untouched.
- **Fix: the optional Config Hub git backup of your agent settings works again** after silently failing to save for several weeks; a failed save is now reported clearly instead of looking healthy.
- **Fix: Config Hub's drift report can now find and repair the "use full file paths" guidance it writes into every agent.** If that file was ever deleted or damaged, the drift report showed nothing wrong and the Repair actions refused it as unrecognised; it now shows up as drift like any other managed file and Overwrite restores it correctly.
- **Improve: copy and paste in the terminal now works properly on iPhone and iPad**, with dedicated on-screen Copy and Paste controls, and desktop gained a matching Copy button.
- **Improve: numerous layout and readability fixes** across the workspace drawer, Settings pages and Activity tray, including clearer buttons, better use of screen width, and fixes for text that was hard to read.

## 2026.07.30.02

- **New: Grok Build and Kimi Code are now available as built-in agents.** Install and launch the latest official stable versions from the Agent Store, with persistent workspaces, account linking inside the running agent, conversation resume, terminal settings, skills, commands, AGENTS.md guidance and Config Hub MCP support.
- **Fix: repeated plugin updates no longer get blocked by a stale installer lock.** The background supervisor now releases the installation lifecycle lock correctly while running agents remain active through routine hot-swap updates.

## 2026.07.21.03

- **Improve: saved workspaces now restart automatically.** Workspaces created in the drawer come back after a server reboot and are recreated after an unexpected agent exit. You can switch automatic restart off for any workspace that should remain stopped.
- **Fix: conversation recovery during plugin maintenance is safer.** Claude and Codex workspace details are captured before a deliberate maintenance stop, and the exact saved conversation is used when the workspace returns instead of silently opening a new one.
- **Fix: Repair now fails safely when storage is ambiguous.** Repair checks the plugin's current storage layout and restores only known-good mounts. It no longer invokes the retired legacy-image rebuild path, interrupts running sessions, or tries to reconstruct storage when the evidence is incomplete.

## 2026.07.19.01

- **Fix: routine plugin updates no longer close or replace running agents.** Updates activate through validated, immutable generations while existing Claude, Codex and other agent sessions keep using the generation they started with. Busy agent upgrades now wait for sessions to close naturally unless you explicitly choose the force action.
- **Fix: conversations reconnect and resume more reliably after an unexpected exit.** Claude and Codex resume information is preserved instead of silently starting a new conversation, and a workspace automatically reconnects when its terminal server has been replaced.
- **Fix: agent update channels now match the selected setting.** Stable resolves the vendor's stable release, Beta resolves prereleases, and pinned versions remain pinned; legacy Latest settings are safely interpreted as Stable.
- **Improve: Markdown and HTML files now open in full preview by default.** Markdown previews render Mermaid diagrams with light/dark theme matching, accessible errors, zoom controls and a scrollable canvas; new files still open for editing.
- **Fix: workspace terminal settings remain scoped to the workspace.** Mouse mode and other tmux settings no longer leak between sessions, and creating a new folder from the workspace picker works again.

## 2026.07.12.01

- **Feat: Workspace config &amp; assets browser.** A new per-workspace view shows every config file the AI agent actually uses — its instructions, skills, commands, hooks, MCP servers and settings — gathered from the agent's home, the project, and parent folders into one collapsible tree you can browse and open.
- **Feat: Built-in file editor.** Click any file in that tree, or a file path shown in a terminal, to open it in an in-page code/markdown editor over the terminal, with live preview. It also opens the agent's own home config files, which Unraid's standard file browser can't reach. A config file you don't have yet shows an "Add" action that creates it the first time you save.
- **Feat: Right-click menu on workspace rows.** Close, Rename (edit the name inline on the row), Config/assets, Session settings, Upload and Export now live in one keyboard-navigable menu, and the small close cross is gone.
- **Improve: Clickable terminal file paths** now also recognise files at the workspace root, and agents are guided to always write workspace-relative paths so those paths stay clickable.

## 2026.07.11.01

- **Feat: click a file path in a terminal to open it in Unraid's editor.** When an AI agent creates or refers to a file — for example `docs/specs/myspec.md` — the path now appears as a link in the terminal. Clicking it opens that file directly in Unraid's built-in file editor, instead of having to track it down by hand under Shares.
- **Feat: paste an image straight into a terminal.** Press Ctrl+V to drop an image into an agent's session. The image is saved into that agent's workspace and its path is handed to the agent automatically — with no upload dialog to click through, and none of the previous clipboard/X11 errors that appeared on a headless server.
- **Feat: pin the workspace drawer open.** You can now keep the workspace list on screen while you work: the terminal makes room and sits beside the drawer instead of being covered by it. The list is fully keyboard-navigable (Tab, arrow keys, Enter to switch), and the terminal / SSH / paste shortcuts tuck neatly into the edge of the drawer.

## 2026.06.27.03

- **Fix: saving a home's changes to storage now shows progress and a clear result.** The home Save button previously opened a dialog that looked like nothing happened — there was no progress indicator, and a slow or failed save could leave it spinning. Saving now reports step-by-step progress in the activity tray (the same as agent saves and storage consolidation), shows a clear message when it can't complete, and explains when your data is safely written to flash but RAM stays in use until that home's open terminal sessions are closed.

## 2026.06.23.01

- **Feat: consolidate an agent's home storage on demand.** Over time an agent's saved changes accumulate as separate layers that hold memory; consolidating merges them back into one. The plugin closes the home's open sessions (keeping your place), merges the layers in the background with progress in the activity tray, then reopens the sessions where you left off. Consolidating a home with sessions open previously could hang.
- **Feat: per-agent auto-launch.** A new per-agent option keeps that agent running in the background and reopens it automatically after a plugin update or a server reboot.
- **Fix: your place in a conversation is now kept when the server or array stops.** Stopping the array, shutting the server down, reinstalling or upgrading the plugin, and migrating storage now capture the current chat — including one you've renamed — before closing, so reopening a workspace resumes where you left off instead of starting fresh. Previously only a normal workspace close did this.
- **Fix: starting several agent upgrades at once could leave some not applied.** Running multiple upgrades together could block one another; each upgrade now completes and its session reopens resumed.
- **Fix: Codex no longer prints sandbox errors in its terminal on Unraid.** The sandbox Codex tries to use depends on a Linux capability Unraid's in-memory root filesystem doesn't provide, so it complained on start. Codex now runs without attempting that sandbox, with its human-approval prompts kept.
- **Improve: the background storage compaction no longer competes with your other workloads.** The process that merges an agent's storage layers now runs at low CPU and disk priority (and on efficiency cores on hybrid CPUs), so it can't slow a running VM or the server.

## 2026.06.17.05

**Config Hub — manage every agent's setup from one place (new)**

- **Feat: Central MCP server management.** Define a Model Context Protocol server once, tick which agents should have it, and the plugin writes each agent's native config in the correct format — Claude, Gemini, Qwen, Codex, OpenCode, Kilo, GitHub Copilot, Factory, Goose, and Antigravity, across JSON, TOML, YAML, and each vendor's own MCP grammar. Edits you make by hand in an agent's own config are detected as drift and never silently overwritten.
- **Feat: Shared global instructions.** Write one instruction document and project it into every agent's instruction file (CLAUDE.md, GEMINI.md, QWEN.md, AGENTS.md, Kilo rules, Goose hints, and more) inside a managed block, so your own content in those files is left untouched. Applying shows an Unraid notification of exactly which agents were added, updated, or removed.
- **Feat: Skills &amp; commands library.** Keep your agent skills and slash commands in one place and project them into every agent that supports them.
- **Feat: Optional git-backed config history.** Version your entire agent configuration in a git repo — local, or pushed to your own http or https remote. Secrets stay out of git automatically: OAuth tokens and the secrets vault are never tracked, and any secret values inside an agent's MCP config are reduced to placeholders in the commit while your working files keep the real values. Your plugin settings and workspace list are versioned too, with a one-click confirmed restore. The gigabytes of agent home data stay on flash where they belong.

**Terminal &amp; copy-paste**

- **Feat: First-class copy-paste.** Copying inside any agent's terminal now reaches your clipboard automatically, with a Paste button and a per-session Mouse toggle in the terminal bar. Shift+drag always selects natively.
- **Feat: Per-agent terminal profiles.** Claude Code's Shift+Enter, escape timing, and extended keys are configured automatically — no hand-tuned tmux settings per agent.
- **Feat: First-run wizard.** Storage choice in plain language, a copy-paste primer, and a per-agent sign-in checklist the first time you open the plugin.

**Storage**

- **Feat: Storage target picker.** Choose where agent data lives from a ranked list of real candidates — appdata pool (recommended), other pools, Unassigned Devices, or the array — with free space and warnings, instead of a raw path box. Unraid 7.3 Internal Boot is detected and treated as durable storage.
- **Feat: Unassigned Devices support**, including disks that mount after boot (the plugin waits and retries rather than failing).
- **Feat: Background mounts.** Opening a workspace no longer freezes the browser while storage mounts; progress streams into the activity tray and the terminal opens when ready.
- **Feat: One-click "Graduate" migration.** When your data is on a durable disk, move it off the flash-protection layering engine onto plain storage — faster, with crash-safe move-then-delete and a 14-day rollback copy.
- **Fix: Storage reliability.** Degraded-storage state now survives reboots, stale defer markers self-clear, manifest reads are safe against torn writes, and FAT32's 4 GiB file-size limit is enforced before writing rather than after.

**Visibility &amp; support**

- **Feat: Activity tray.** Installs, upgrades, storage operations, and session starts report step-by-step progress in a non-blocking tray on every page, with stall detection and retry.
- **Feat: Health indicator.** A live green/amber/red chip in the header runs quick self-checks (supervisor, manifest, mounts, disk space, boot integrity) with one-time Unraid notifications on trouble and an optional scheduled check.
- **Feat: Support bundle.** One click builds a redacted diagnostics zip — secret values are scrubbed and the build refuses to ship if any survive — plus copy-ready forum text, a prefilled GitHub issue link, and an opt-in known-issues checker.
- **Feat: Workspace export/import.** Bundle a workspace's settings (secrets excluded by default) and import it onto another path or another server.
- **Improve: Richer diagnostics.** A trace id follows each action from the browser through to the storage scripts, the Debug Console gained context/level/trace filters, and the debug log now rotates instead of growing without bound.

## 2026.06.09.01
- **Fix: the "Storage Attention Needed" warning is now much more accurate.** In some cases it appeared on a workspace whose data was completely intact, and once shown it could linger even after the problem had already cleared. The plugin now confirms a workspace's saved data is genuinely incomplete before warning, and clears the warning automatically as soon as the workspace is healthy again — while still reliably detecting and flagging genuine loss of your most recent work.

## 2026.06.07.02
- **Fix: closing a workspace now shuts the agent down cleanly instead of briefly relaunching it.** When you closed a workspace whose agent had just started (for example a fresh Claude Code session), the agent could be relaunched for a few seconds before the plugin force-closed it. Closing is now clean and immediate, with no flicker of the session coming back.

## 2026.06.07.01
- **Fix: running agents as a non-root user now works.** When the plugin is configured to run agents as a normal (non-root) user, starting a session failed with a "Permission denied" error because part of that user's home folder was created owned by root. The plugin now makes sure the session's own user owns its state folder, so non-root sessions start cleanly.

## 2026.06.06.01
- **Fix: terminals no longer get stuck in a reconnect loop that slowly bogs the server down.** When a workspace terminal's connection dropped and re-established (for example after a browser tab was left in the background), each reconnection left the previous one behind. Those orphaned connections piled up, multiplying the terminal's drawing work and steadily driving up CPU. Each reconnection now cleanly replaces the previous one, so exactly one connection stays live per session.

## 2026.06.05.02
- **Fix: the plugin's background storage service no longer repeatedly restarts itself after an upgrade.** In a specific timing window during a plugin upgrade the service could lose track of its own status and get relaunched over and over (more noticeable with workspaces open), wasting CPU. It now re-confirms its own status each cycle so a single instance stays running.

## 2026.06.05.01
- **Fix: agents now reliably resume your last conversation after an upgrade — for every agent type.** Previously a workspace could reopen to a blank session after an agent upgrade (most visible with Claude Code). Resume now works across every agent, not just some.
- **Fix: stopping the array is now reliable even when the running-session list is momentarily unreadable.** The earlier fix registered the array-stop handler, but the array could still hang if the list of open sessions couldn't be read at that instant. The plugin now releases the array using the same low-level signal the kernel itself uses, so a lingering agent process can no longer hold "user shares" open and block the stop.

## 2026.06.02.10
- **Fix: Stopping the array now reliably closes running agent sessions instead of hanging.** The handler that shuts agents down before the array unmounts was never actually being triggered by Unraid, so an array stop could stall indefinitely on "user share(s) still busy" while agent sessions held the share open. The handler is now correctly registered and fires on every array stop and shutdown.
- **Fix: The drawer's SSH connect button now works over a plain-HTTP connection.** Clicking the key/clipboard tab did nothing when the Unraid GUI is accessed over HTTP. It now opens a panel with the ready-to-use SSH command. Where the browser allows it the command is copied automatically; on an insecure (HTTP) connection — where browsers block automatic copy — the panel clearly says so and lets you click to select the command, with a hint showing the right shortcut for your platform (⌘C on Mac, Ctrl+C elsewhere).
- **Feat: Manually persist an agent's in-memory storage from the Resources tab.** When an agent has unsaved changes held in RAM, its Resources panel now shows a Consolidate button reporting how much is unsaved, so you can flush it to disk on demand rather than waiting for the next scheduled save.

## 2026.06.02.04
- **Fix: Upgrading multiple agents at the same time could silently leave one agent's new installation only in RAM, with no Flash backup.** If a second upgrade started while another was still running, it could fail with "Install Failed" and leave the newly-installed agent version unprotected — a server reboot would lose it entirely. The install sequence now always writes a Flash backup even when the full layer compaction step has to wait, so the data is safe regardless of timing.

## 2026.06.02.02
- **Fix: Stopping the Unraid array now correctly waits for running agent sessions to close.** The array-stop sequence now shuts down active agents (Claude Code, Antigravity CLI, Gemini CLI, etc.) before allowing `/mnt/user` to unmount, so the array stop completes cleanly instead of retrying indefinitely.
- **Fix: Session settings (tmux, workspace) save reliably after the plugin flushes RAM to disk.** A storage maintenance step was removing a directory entry from RAM that subsequent writes depended on, causing a "Save failed" error in the Manage Session overlay.
- **Fix: Agents installed before a reboot now show their correct installed status.** The installed-agent detector wasn't recognising the current storage layer naming format, causing recently-installed agents to appear as "not installed" after a restart.

## 2026.06.01.01
- **Improve: lighter plugin upgrades.** A routine upgrade no longer performs a redundant save-to-disk of in-memory data — that data is already protected and is written to disk on the normal schedule — so an upgrade does a little less flash I/O and finishes cleaner.

## 2026.05.31.08
- **Improve (data durability): stronger guarantees that your conversation history is safe before RAM is reclaimed.** Building on the v2026.05.31.07 fix, the plugin now reclaims a file from RAM only once it has been *proven* written to a storage layer — so a save that didn't capture a file can never lead to that file being discarded — and storage consolidation now refuses to run from an incomplete view of your saved layers (which could otherwise drop data). Together these close the conversation-loss issue at its root, for every agent, rather than by listing known file locations.

## 2026.05.31.07
- **Fix (data loss — important): agent conversation history could be lost during storage maintenance or a plugin upgrade.** The routine that reclaims RAM after saving to Flash could, in certain timing windows, delete an agent's conversation files (Claude, Antigravity, and others) from RAM before they were durably written to Flash — and an upgrade performed while a session was active could proceed without first flushing recent conversations. Both are now fixed: conversation/chat-history files are never reclaimed from RAM, and an upgrade always flushes your unsaved work to Flash first. **Already-lost history is not recoverable by upgrading.** If you are on v2026.05.31.06, please update to this release as soon as possible.

## 2026.05.31.06
- **Feat: Automatic memory reclaim for long-lived workspaces.** When a workspace stays open long enough to build up unsaved changes in RAM and the plugin needs that memory back (storage pressure, or many pending storage layers), it now warns you and counts down 5 minutes, then gracefully closes the session — saving your place so you can reopen and resume exactly where you left off.
- **Fix: Agent commands no longer intermittently fail with "No such file or directory" during a live session.** While the plugin saved a workspace's RAM to disk, a refresh could briefly remount your home directory out from under a running agent (for example Claude Code creating a session folder). The save no longer disturbs a connected session.
- **Fix: Antigravity CLI now reopens to your last conversation** instead of a blank one — the plugin reads agy's own conversation index when you reopen a workspace.
- **Fix: Tools an agent runs for you — git, editors, pagers — no longer hang** waiting for input that never arrives; they now run non-interactively and complete.
- **Fix: Interactive prompts inside a full-screen agent render cleanly.** A prompt such as an SSH password requested by a tool running inside a TUI agent no longer "staircases" diagonally down the screen.
- **Fix: The copied SSH connect command now actually attaches.** The one-click "copy SSH command" produced a command that reported "no sessions" because it didn't point at the plugin's private tmux socket; it now connects to your live session.
- **Improve: The plugin UI now follows your Unraid light or dark theme** — panels, bars, and dialogs adapt instead of always rendering dark. (The debug/log console stays dark on purpose — it's a terminal.)
- **Improve: "Keep a copy on upgrade" now defaults to off** — a backup is a deliberate opt-in — and the option gently pulses while unticked so it's easy to spot.

## 2026.05.24.03
- **Fix: Antigravity CLI sessions displayed corrupted terminal output on first launch.** Go's internal log messages were being written directly to the terminal, overlapping with the agent's own display. The log directory the agent uses to redirect those messages away from the screen now exists before the agent starts.
- **Fix: Agent could fail on first launch with an authentication error after a full sync to persistent storage** (complete fix — v2026.05.24.02 contained the right logic but an unrelated packaging issue meant the fix was not installed on upgrade; this release ensures it lands correctly).

## 2026.05.24.02
- **Fix: Agent could fail on first launch with an authentication error after a full sync to persistent storage.** After a clean complete bake, the post-sync cleanup routine was inadvertently removing the overlay's working directory from the filesystem. The overlay appeared mounted and reads worked fine, but all writes — including the OAuth token refresh that runs at every startup — returned "No such file or directory", causing agents to report auth errors or loop on launch. Fixed.

## 2026.05.24.01
- **Fix (data loss — important): the proper fix for agents forgetting your sessions.** v2026.05.18.08 announced a fix for this — that release tackled one symptom but missed the underlying cause. Your agent (Copilot, OpenCode, Codex, Kilo Code, Goose) could still occasionally start as if it had never seen you before, or hang on the "Waking..." loading screen. This release fixes the underlying behaviour. **Already-lost session history is not recoverable by upgrading.** If an agent now hangs at Waking or complains about a corrupted database, in the affected agent's directory (e.g. `~/.codex/`, `~/.copilot/`) delete any `.db-shm` or `.db-wal` files that don't have a matching `.db` next to them, then re-launch — the agent starts fresh.
- **Fix: Agent commands no longer occasionally fail mid-storage-save.** On busy servers, a command running in the brief window when the plugin was saving RAM to persistent storage could fail with "No such file or directory" — most reproducible on a clean Antigravity install. The save and the launch no longer collide.
- **Security: Tighter checks on agent installs.** Downloaded agent packages are now signature-verified before being unpacked, and downloads must use HTTPS. Defence-in-depth — nothing observable in normal use.
- **Improve: Tidier cleanup when an install fails.** A failed agent install no longer leaves behind hidden host resources, so the host stays clean across many transient failures.

## 2026.05.23.19
- **Feat: Antigravity CLI added.** Google's coding assistant is now in the Agent Store. Tracks upstream versions for the update card, and supports Resume from a specific conversation or the most recent.
- **Feat: Keep-a-copy on upgrade.** Optionally retain a per-version backup of an agent's layers when upgrading. The version picker grows a "Restore" option listing the kept backups; pick one to roll back to that version. The upgrade dialog shows disk usage up-front so you can decide whether to keep a copy. Backups live alongside the active layers in your configured persistence path.
- **Feat: Native keyring for agents that ask for one.** Agents that store their auth tokens in a system keyring previously re-prompted for auth every session because Unraid has no keyring daemon. The plugin now starts a per-user keyring at agent launch, so the token survives across sessions. Today this benefits Antigravity CLI; the framework is generic.
- **Feat: Agent CLIs work from the Unraid host terminal after a reboot.** Running an agent CLI from the standard Unraid Terminal button right after a reboot previously failed with "No such file or directory" — agent storage was only attached on demand when the plugin's own webterm opened. The plugin now attaches every installed agent at array start, so the binaries are available to any shell on the host immediately.
- **Fix: Setting "Terminal User" to a non-root account now works end-to-end.** Previously the Settings dropdown saved the wrong value, the agent's home was effectively read-only, terminals failed to launch, and the Store-card panels kept showing the previous user's data after the switch. All four issues are fixed, and the Settings page auto-reloads on user-switch so per-user data re-renders against the new home. All close, agent-upgrade, hard-stop, plugin-stop, plugin-uninstall, and array-stop paths now reach non-root sessions too.
- **Fix: "Terminal session not found" after a busy server tick.** Other processes on the host can occasionally leave the shared tmux socket directory with permissions tmux rejects, and every plugin terminal would then fail to start. The plugin now uses its own private socket directory, isolated from anything else on the box.
- **Fix: Agent-upgrade "open sessions" count no longer inflated by orphan terminals.** Failed launches and unclean exits previously left terminal-server processes alive forever. The upgrade-confirm dialog counted these as live sessions, inflating the warning. The plugin now reconciles terminal-server processes against running sessions on every list and array-start, and reaps orphans automatically.
- **Fix: Resume button now appears for Antigravity CLI workspaces after close + re-add.** The close-time resume-id capture wasn't aware of agy's specific exit behaviour or where it stores its conversation files; both handled now. Note: agy itself still requires two Ctrl-Ds to exit — that's upstream behaviour, not something the plugin can change.
- **Fix: Claude Resume cross-workspace contamination.** Closing workspace B sometimes saved workspace A's session id, so clicking Resume on B later opened Claude with the wrong session and refused with "No conversation found". Resume-id discovery is now scoped to the closing workspace.
- **Fix: CLI Args panel reflects the active Terminal User.** After switching the Terminal User in Settings, the per-agent Args panel kept showing the previous user's saved arg until the page was hard-refreshed. The Settings page now auto-reloads on a user-switch.
- **Improve: Release-notes link + A-Z sort on the Agent Store.** Each Store card now shows a Release-notes link when the agent's source publishes a changelog URL. The agent grid gets an A-Z/Z-A toggle, persisted in the URL.

## 2026.05.18.08
- **Fix (data loss — important): your agents stop forgetting your sessions.** A long-standing bug in how the plugin saves data from RAM to your Flash drive could silently drop the session-history database files used by Codex CLI, GitHub Copilot, Kilo Code, OpenCode and Goose — so an agent would occasionally start as if it had never seen you before, or hang on the "Waking Codex CLI..." loading screen. In severe cases the whole Unraid dashboard could freeze for minutes when the plugin was in use (downstream effect of an agent stuck reading a half-deleted database). This release fixes the save routine and adds defence-in-depth checks. **Already-lost session history is not recoverable by upgrading.** If an agent now hangs at Waking or complains about a corrupted database, in the affected agent's directory (e.g. `~/.codex/`, `~/.copilot/`) delete any `.db-shm` or `.db-wal` files that don't have a matching `.db` next to them, then re-launch — the agent starts fresh.
- **Improve: Plugin upgrades no longer interrupt your work.** Routine upgrades from this release forward leave your terminal sessions running and your agents in place — typical upgrade time drops from ~30–90s of session-killing teardown to ~5–15s. The longer path is still used (and the release notes will say so) when a release genuinely needs to rebuild your storage layout. **One-time exception:** the upgrade FROM the previous storefront TO this release will still take the long path, because this release introduces the marker the plugin uses to recognise compatible layouts. From the next upgrade onward, routine updates run uninterrupted. Unsaved RAM data is flushed to Flash just before the swap, so a sudden power loss during the brief upgrade window doesn't lose recent activity.
- **Improve: Qwen Code's DashScope API key now appears as a labelled password field on the agent's Store card** — previously users had to discover the `DASHSCOPE_API_KEY` env variable name themselves from the qwen-code README. Alternative providers (Ollama, vLLM, …) can still be configured via the general env panel.

## 2026.05.18.05
- Fix (data loss): Storage consolidation no longer deletes the `.gemini/tmp/` directory during its pre-bake prune. That path holds gemini-cli's per-project session chat logs (`.gemini/tmp/&lt;projectId&gt;/chats/session-*.jsonl`) — durable user state, not cache. The previous behaviour was silently wiping chat history on every consolidate, and crashing the next gemini launch with an ENOENT on the session log. If you've used gemini-cli with this plugin before this release, past chat history is unfortunately not recoverable; from this release forward, it persists. (Verified on the test box: a synthetic chat log survives a full consolidate with content intact.)
- Fix: Workspace session resume now works correctly for Kilo Code, Pi Coder, GitHub Copilot, and Goose. The resume flags wired into the "attach to existing session" command had drifted from each agent's current upstream CLI:
  - Kilo Code: `resume_latest` now passes `--continue` (previously plain `{binary} {args}`, which started a new session). Per-ID resume uses `--session &lt;id&gt;` (canonical form of `-s`).
  - Pi Coder: `resume_latest` now uses `--continue` (previously `--resume`, which opens an interactive picker that hangs in the SSH-attach flow with no TTY input). Per-ID resume uses `--session &lt;id&gt;`.
  - GitHub Copilot CLI: `resume_latest` now uses `--continue` (previously plain `{binary} {args}`). Per-ID resume keeps `--resume=&lt;id&gt;`.
  - Goose: per-ID resume now uses `session --resume -n &lt;id&gt;` (previously `session --name &lt;id&gt;`, which CREATED a new session named `&lt;id&gt;` instead of resuming an existing one).
- Fix: OpenCode is detected as installed reliably. The plugin's installed-state check was looking at `bin/opencode`, but the npm package ships `bin/opencode.exe` (a cross-platform naming convention also used by Claude Code — the postinstall replaces the file with the platform-matched binary). The agent worked anyway via the resolved `node_modules/.bin/opencode` symlink, but the inconsistency could surface as "INSTALL" reappearing on the Store card under some refresh paths.

## 2026.05.18.02
- Improve: Storage consolidation no longer trips on busy workspaces. When the boot integrity / auto-consolidation pass runs while a workspace has files open on the home mount, the plugin now defers the operation (with a clear "deferred — busy" log) instead of marking it a failure and counting it against the auto-halt threshold. The Storage tab also gains a small non-blocking banner if a real consolidate failure happens, so it surfaces at the first occurrence rather than only after the supervisor escalates to a halt. When a failure does happen, the last 50 lines of the debug log are now snapshotted to `/boot/config/plugins/unraid-aicliagents/failures/` and the stderr tail is inlined into the lifecycle log entry, so the cause survives `/tmp` rotation between the failure and the next time anyone looks.
- Fix: Agent channel selections (and other Settings writes that go through the atomic writer) reliably persist across a page reload on heavily-loaded servers. The atomic-write path now disables the userland buffer and fsyncs before the rename, closing a cross-process visibility lag that occasionally made the beta-channel radio appear unchecked immediately after saving.

## 2026.05.17.02
- Improve: Out of beta. The plugin now ships as a regular Community Applications release — the Beta flag in the CA template has been removed.
- Fix: Codex CLI launches correctly after install. From `@openai/codex` v0.99, OpenAI split the native binary into a per-platform optional dependency, so the previous expected binary path was wrong and Codex crashed immediately with "Agent Binary Missing". The path is now correct, and a fallback preserves pre-v0.99 installs that haven't been reinstalled.
- Improve: Agent-storage halts now self-heal silently. If the boot integrity check finds an agent's binary layers missing, the plugin automatically re-runs the install (agent storage is just npm code — there's nothing to lose) instead of presenting a scary "Storage Unavailable — start fresh and abandon data" prompt. Real user-data halts (home storage) keep their destructive confirmation, but the WIPE dialog now actually has an input box (previously the gate was decorative, and Cancel looped back to the same overlay with no escape). Every halt card also gains a Retry-integrity-check button and a Dismiss-for-24h button, so the destructive path is never the only escape.
- Improve: Halt overlay follows the active Unraid theme (light / dark / auto) instead of forcing a dark+orange palette that didn't blend with the rest of the UI.
- Fix: Uninstalling an agent now cleans up its layer-manifest entry and clears any pending halt sentinel. Without this, the next reboot's integrity sweep treated the just-uninstalled agent as "all expected layers missing" and surfaced a phantom Storage Unavailable halt for an agent that wasn't even on disk anymore.

## 2026.05.15.16
- Feat: Connect to workspace terminals from your local SSH client. A new "SSH Keys" card in Settings registers a public key for tmux-attach access; clicking the key icon on any workspace row copies a ready-to-paste `ssh user@host -t "tmux attach …"` command (UTF-8 locale prefixed so agent status glyphs render correctly). Recommended on Windows: Windows Terminal, not the legacy "Windows PowerShell" host. A key registered in one browser is recognised across every browser pointed at the same Unraid box.
- Fix: Agent Marketplace no longer shows "No agents match the current filter" while matching cards are visible above (an empty-state race during the initial grid render).
- Fix: SSH Key Setup modal renders cleanly on Unraid 7.2.x — the close button, OS tabs, and command-copy buttons no longer appear as orange-bordered rectangles.
- Improve: "Saving session to Flash drive" overlay and the workspace Secrets card now say "persistent storage" — clearer wording that doesn't expose where the data physically lives.

## 2026.05.12.06
- Fix: Upgrading an agent no longer occasionally fails with "Install Failed (Bake Error)". Two storage-bakes of the same agent could race during an upgrade (one finishing its remount while the other was mid-bake); a per-agent lock now serializes them, and a redundant duplicate bake on agent install was removed.

## 2026.05.12.05
- Improve: Reduced Flash-drive (USB stick) write wear. The storage layer now syncs to Flash on a gentler cadence (a ~2-hour default window instead of 30 minutes), consolidates its SquashFS layers far less often, and no longer writes regenerable agent caches to Flash at all — the npm cache, `~/.cache`, agent temp/telemetry directories, etc. are excluded from the bake. Net effect: the plugin writes a lot less to your USB stick. Storage that's currently carrying that cache cruft is slimmed down automatically on the next layer consolidation. (Migrated/backup data is never touched by this — clear that via the storage tab's recovery card if you want it gone.)

## 2026.05.12.02
- Fix: Upgrading an agent while one of its workspace sessions is open no longer strands that session. Some agents (e.g. Claude Code 2.1.x) have replaced their legacy "cli.js" entry point with a native binary; the launch now re-checks the agent's binary on every relaunch rather than using the path resolved when the session was opened, so an in-place upgrade is picked up automatically. (If a session was already stranded by such an upgrade, close and reopen that workspace once and it will pick up the new binary.)
- Improve: After a plugin install or upgrade, the agent Store cards now show each uninstalled agent's available version straight away — a background version-cache refresh runs on install, so you no longer have to press "Check for Updates" first.

## 2026.05.12.01
- Feat: Environment &amp; secrets management. Every agent's Store card and every workspace now has an "Environment" panel covering general env vars AND API keys/secrets, with full add / edit / delete for both. Secrets are masked and stored separately under tightened (0600) permissions; general vars are managed more loosely. Per-workspace values override the per-agent defaults, and values apply automatically to newly opened terminal sessions ("hot-apply") with no workspace rebuild. Agents that ship default env vars seed them on install as an editable starting set. Replaces the old hardcoded-only API-key vault (the Config-tab "Secrets Vault" card is removed); clearing a value via the UI now actually clears it.
- Feat: Per-agent and per-workspace CLI arguments. A new "Args" panel on each Store card sets default extra flags for that agent (e.g. --max-turns 5), and a workspace can override them in its drawer. Arguments are validated against shell metacharacters. Changing args while a session is open offers "Apply now" — the agent is reloaded in place (Ctrl-C + relaunch) with the new flags, no destroy/recreate.
- Feat: Auto-launch workspaces. A per-workspace toggle in the Terminal panel marks a workspace to start its session automatically — on page load, and after an agent install or upgrade — so your usual workspaces come back without clicking through.
- Feat: Agent Store cards redesigned. Each agent is now one card with five progressive-disclosure panels: Channel, Environment/Secrets, Runtime (RAM, storage stats), Terminal (tmux), and Storage. tmux settings have four tiers of precedence — built-in then agent default then workspace override then a .conf escape hatch — with only divergent keys persisted. Per-agent secret schemas can carry multiple fields (Goose, for instance, registers Provider / Model / provider keys).
- Feat: Two new agents — Goose (Block) and Qwen Code — plus a new agent-source framework so the plugin can manage tools that aren't published to npm (GitHub-release binaries, curl-installers, tarballs), not just npm packages.
- Feat: Workspace resume. Closing a workspace from the drawer now captures the agent's resume id — a printed UUID, a named session, or, for agents like OpenCode that print nothing, the most recent id from their own session database — and offers a "Resume" button next to "Start Fresh" the next time you open a session on that path. Wide tmux capture plus retries so long resume lines aren't truncated.
- Feat: Graceful agent upgrades. Installing or upgrading an agent now enumerates and cleanly closes the active workspace sessions for that agent first (preserving each session's resume id) before swapping the binary, instead of yanking it out from under running terminals. The install/upgrade button warns you with the list of sessions that will be closed; the New Workspace overlay greys out agents whose install is in progress; the install-progress panel appears immediately on click.
- Feat: Cold-start loading overlay. The terminal shows a spinner, the agent icon and a "Starting [agent]..." message for the whole cold-start window (most of which is the agent's own startup) instead of a blank terminal, dismissing as soon as the agent produces output.
- Improve: Storage robustness overhaul. A background storage daemon now owns all SquashFS bake/consolidate work, so the UI never blocks on storage I/O and the "syncing..." indicator clears reliably (it polls real state instead of guessing on a timer). Every layer write is atomic and checksum-verified. On boot your persisted layers are integrity-checked: corruption, missing layers, or a path/host mismatch is detected, you're notified, workspace access is held until it's resolved, and — where a copy survives in a backup/migrated sibling directory — a one-click "Restore" rebuilds from it. Un-baked data is monitored with graduated thresholds. Fixed a class of silent data loss where resume ids, workspace records or agent credentials written during a consolidation cycle could be discarded when the in-memory layer was wiped after the bake. Auto-consolidation now defers while the terminal is busy and runs when idle, so deltas no longer pile up indefinitely on the home stack. Writes to the Flash drive — API keys, plugin config, layer manifests — are forced to disk on every change so they survive an abrupt reboot instead of lingering in the OS page cache. The old per-user sync daemon is retired.
- Fix: ZRAM storage initialisation now works on Unraid 7.2.x and other kernels where zram is built in — a capability probe (/sys/class/zram-control, /dev/zram0) replaces the fatal modprobe zram, with an mkfs.xfs fallback when mkfs.ext4-on-block-device isn't available. Resolves the install failure reported in GitHub issue #5.
- Fix: Agent version display. The Plugins "Update" card and the Store-card version badge showed v0.0.0 / "v?" for most installed agents on a fresh boot, because version discovery was reading package.json from an overlay that wasn't mounted yet. It now mounts on demand and reads the real semver, and a one-shot backfill repairs the registry on upgrade. The version picker also now filters pre-release tags out of the Stable channel correctly and reliably installs the version you pick — downgrade, reinstall and pick-specific-version were no-ops on the redesigned cards.
- Fix: Persistence paths on custom Unraid pools (ZFS pools, user-named cache pools) are accepted instead of rejected with a misleading "outside allowed prefixes" error; stopping the array is no longer blocked by terminals holding a working directory under /mnt/user (the array-stop event is handled, not just full shutdown); installed agents resolve on the main Unraid shell and web terminal (goose, qwen etc. wrappers in /usr/local/bin, and the workspace terminal PATH includes every installed agent's bin directory).
- Fix: UI polish — web fonts now load (the @import was mid-stylesheet, which browsers silently drop); Chrome no longer autofills the agent search box with "root" and hides every card; the "Leave site?" dialog no longer pops when navigating away from the terminal tab; the Plugins page now shows the support-thread link and a plugin description.
- Fix: Per-agent launch reliability — Claude Code's native binary layout, Codex-CLI's vendored Rust binary, OpenCode's cache-directory creation, Goose's first-run TUI prompt, Qwen Code's binary path, and fast-exit handling so a mis-configured agent shows its error instead of relaunch-looping; Node and npm caches are kept on tmpfs and never written to the Flash drive; broadened post-install cleanup of stale /tmp artifacts; XML-escaping fixes in the installer/uninstaller hooks.

## 2026.04.16.27
- Fix: Migration script wrote home sqsh to agent_storage_path instead of home_storage_path. When paths differ (common for users with persistence_base configured), the home sqsh was placed where only agents are expected, causing mount failure. Now reads home_storage_path and persistence_base from config separately. Also searches all relevant paths for legacy IMG files and raw folders.

## 2026.04.16.26
- Fix: Background migration hung the installer UI. The nohup backgrounded process kept file descriptors open, preventing the PLG install script from exiting. Added disown after the background launch to fully detach the migration process from the installer shell.

## 2026.04.16.25
- Fix: Removed test-harness.sh download from PLG. The dev test script was excluded from the public GitHub repo but still referenced as a FILE download in the PLG, causing install failure on production servers pulling from GitHub.

## 2026.04.16.24 - The "Storage Intelligence" Update
- Feat: SquashFS Storage Architecture - Replaced Btrfs loopback images with a layered SquashFS + ZRAM overlay system. Agent binaries and home directories now use compressed read-only layers with a RAM write buffer, dramatically reducing Flash USB wear while maintaining instant persistence. Automatic layer consolidation keeps storage footprint minimal.
- Feat: Array-Aware Storage - The plugin now detects when configured storage paths depend on the Unraid array or pools. When the array is stopped, a Storage Unavailable overlay guides users through emergency options. When the array starts, the plugin automatically restores normal operation with no manual intervention needed.
- Feat: Emergency Mode - When all storage is on the stopped array, users can install a temporary AI agent directly into RAM and launch an emergency terminal session. OpenCode is recommended as it requires no authentication. Temporary agents and sessions are automatically cleaned up when the array restarts.
- Feat: Agent Version Management - Replaced the simple Stable/Preview toggle with a full version picker dropdown per agent. Browse all available versions with tagged releases and stable versions within a configurable time window. Supports upgrade, downgrade, and channel selection (latest, next, beta, etc). Update notifications appear via Unraid built-in notification system on a configurable schedule.
- Feat: Configurable Storage Locations - Home and agent storage paths can now be independently configured and migrated between Flash, array shares, cache pools, and unassigned devices. A guided migration flow persists data, copies files with progress tracking, and consolidates at the destination.
- Feat: Array Stop Warning - When stopping the array, a warning dialog lists affected AI sessions and storage paths. Users can choose to proceed (sessions are terminated gracefully) or cancel. Sessions on non-array paths continue running uninterrupted.
- Feat: Docker Tool Wrappers - Integrated proxy scripts for Docker-based tools (e.g. semgrep). When an agent requests a tool, it transparently runs via Docker container with clear install instructions if the image is not available.
- Improve: Settings Page Performance - The Agent Store tab no longer blocks on npm registry queries during page load. Version data is cached and refreshed in the background, making the settings page load instantly.
- Improve: Install Progress Resilience - Agent install and update progress bars now survive page refreshes. If you navigate away and return during an installation, the progress bar resumes from where it left off.
- Improve: Storage Migration Safety - Consolidation is skipped when source or target is on Flash USB to avoid unnecessary write amplification. Config file writes are serialized to prevent corruption from concurrent operations.
- Improve: Real-Time Status Updates - Storage status changes (array start/stop) are detected via Nchan for instant UI updates, with a polling fallback for reliability. Page reloads no longer trigger the browser unsaved changes dialog.
- Fix: Terminal clipboard and right-click behavior restored to browser defaults.
- Fix: Storage path availability detection now correctly identifies when array shares are inaccessible.
- Fix: Home storage path setting now correctly applies to home operations.

## 2026.04.06.54
- Feat: Full-Screen Terminal Overlay - Added a dedicated 'Temporary Terminal' accessible directly from the agent drawer. This provides a blur-backed, full-screen bash session synchronized with your active workspace directory for manual CLI operations.
- Feat: Ready-Now Workspace Performance - Implemented 'Boot-time Resurrection' which proactively pre-loads all AI agent binaries and user home RAM volumes during system startup or installation. This eliminates the restoration delay previously encountered on first use.
- Improve: Terminal-to-Workspace Synchronization - Switching between workspace tabs now automatically reloads all terminal sessions (both overlay and tab-based) to ensure the path always matches the visible project.
- Improve: Btrfs Storage Resilience - Hardened the agent storage lifecycle with mandatory auto-mounting and namespace verification, ensuring reliable binary availability even after unexpected system reboots.
- Improve: UI Initialization Feedback - Added a descriptive 'Restoring Home Storage' overlay to the terminal interface to provide users with visual status during the first background restoration of persistent data to RAM.
- Fix: Loopback Image Stability - Optimized the Btrfs storage floor and headroom constraints to prevent 'No space left' (ENOSPC) errors during image resizing, and ensured storage locks are correctly enforced after maintenance cycles.

## 2026.04.04.05
- Improve: Storage Intelligence - Implemented advanced Btrfs management including tail-block evacuation for reliable image shrinking, intelligent expansion guards to protect Flash drive headroom, and automated self-healing for corrupted loopback images.
- Improve: UI &amp; UX Refinement - Redesigned the Agent Store and configuration drawers with a high-density layout, improved spacing, and automated drawer management for a smoother workspace transition.
- Improve: Terminal Resilience - Significantly hardened terminal session stability and connection reliability through improved user isolation and robust environment variable propagation.
- Improve: Diagnostics &amp; Transparency - Enhanced the storage dashboard with "Truthful Capacity Reporting" showing both logical data size and physical disk footprint, along with better error visibility for system maintenance tasks.
- Fix: Storage Permissions - Resolved edge cases where agent storage could become write-protected or inaccessible due to kernel-level loopback locks.

## 2026.03.28.05
- Improve: Data Integrity - Implemented SQLite 'Surgical Repair' (PRAGMA integrity_check) and automated pre-flight recovery for OpenCode and Claude agent databases.
- Improve: Performance - Drastically reduced plugin upgrade time and periodic sync latency on USB Flash drives by implementing '--size-only' rsync and excluding non-essential caches (.npm, .bun).
- Security: Replaced 'eval' command execution with safe Bash array-based execution in the terminal wrapper to eliminate arbitrary code execution risks.
- Fix: PHP 8.0+ Compatibility - Resolved 'unlink' warnings and improved custom error handling to correctly respect the suppression operator (@).
- Fix: Upgrade Reliability - Added automated RAM-to-Flash backup and SQLite 'wal_checkpoint' during plugin updates to ensure zero data loss.

## 2026.03.27.20
- Fix: Critical XML Validation (Escapes raw ampersands in changelogs to resolve 'XML parse error' failures).
- Fix: Switched to high-fidelity literal replacement logic for public releases to prevent corrupted .plg structure.

## 2026.03.27.19
- Feat: Added Shell Integration aliases for all agents (kilo, pi, codex, droid, nanocoder).
- Fix: Resolved 'Status not available' by fixing GitHub URL extraction for SSH-over-443 remotes.
- Fix: Corrected changelog replacement to prevent symbol corruption during publishing.

## 2026.03.27.18
- Feat: Added Support for OpenCode, Claude Code, and NanoCoder agents.
- Feat: Global Shell Integration providing native 'claude', 'gemini', and 'opencode' aliases in all SSH and local terminal sessions.
- Feat: Integrated "User &amp; Architecture Guide" links within the Settings page and Terminal Drawer for instant help access.
- Improve: Terminal Stability with optimized shell environment propagation and automated SQLite self-healing for agent history.
- Fix: Reinforced recursive permission enforcement for agent binaries to prevent 'Permission denied' / EACCES errors in RAM.

## 2026.03.18.01
- Feat: Added Factory CLI (@factory/cli) support
- Feat: Integrated 'droid' binary and Factory session management
- UI: Added Factory icon and updated agent registry

## 2026.03.17.35 - The "Professional Workspace" Update
- Feat: Advanced Workspace Environment Management - New "Manage ENV" drawer overlay allows viewing and overriding global API keys per workspace without affecting global settings.
- Feat: Intelligent API Persistence - Dynamically discovers and persists API keys for all installed agents (OpenCode, Kilo Code, etc.) in the Secrets Vault.
- Feat: Hybrid Home Persistence - Implemented a decoupled background sync daemon that asynchronously mirrors the high-performance RAM home directory to the Flash drive.
- Feat: Multi-User Migration - Seamlessly migrates AI agent data when switching the active Unraid user, ensuring chat history is preserved.
- Improve: Premium UI Theming - Unified orange button theme, consistent card layouts, and professional blue-sidebar help styling throughout the manager.
- Improve: Performance &amp; Stability - Optimized terminal initialization to eliminate 502 Bad Gateway errors and implemented atomic locking for background sync operations.
- Improve: Clipboard Synchronization - Enabled OSC 52 support for dual-direction clipboard synchronization between the AI terminal and your browser.
- Improve: TrueColor Support - Full 24-bit TrueColor environment propagation across the entire terminal stack for better syntax highlighting.
- Fix: Terminal Rendering - Resolved scrolling and corruption issues in terminal sessions, particularly for limited-user contexts.
- Fix: Setting Persistence - Ensured fallback API keys and backup schedule settings correctly persist between reboots and user changes.
- Fix: Environment Visibility - Resolved a critical bug where custom environment variables and Secrets Vault keys were not correctly propagated to the active AI agent.

## 2026.03.09.19 - The "Premium UX" Update
- Feat: Expanded Agent Store - Added support for Claude Code, OpenCode, Kilo Code, Pi Coder, and Codex CLI.
- Feat: Integrated Node.js Environment - Bundled Node.js (v22.22.0) with npm for seamless, portable agent management.
- Feat: Premium Uninstaller UI - Completely redesigned uninstallation with quiet logging and a resilient, high-contrast summary box confirming preservation of settings and chats.
- Feat: Premium Installer UX - Polished installation flow with professional status updates and a new "INSTALL COMPLETE" visual summary.
- Improve: System Branding - Unified all system notifications and UI elements under the "AI CLI Agents Plugin" title.
- Improve: Boot Resiliency - Implemented persistent USB source caching for instant UI availability on reboot.
- Improve: Hardware Optimization - Moved all runtime logs to RAM (/tmp) to minimize USB flash drive wear.
</CHANGES>


